    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Management-Engineering-_R00024049": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Business Developer)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nRRIS (Rehabilitation Research Institute of Singapore) We bring together expertise from three key areas: academic research through NTU, science and technology through A*STAR, and healthcare through NHG. This integrated approach allows us to leverage diverse strengths to develop innovative solutions for clinical challenges. The Research Associate will bridge technical and commercial requirements to develop viable solutions for a novel rehabilitation robot. This role involves collaborating with stakeholders to refine and implement cutting-edge haptic technologies integrated into robotic solutions helping translate research concepts into viable and impactful solutions. Key Responsibilities: Assist in planning, tracking, and executing project activities. Establish effective communication to ensure seamless execution. Conduct market research to identify industry trends and stakeholder needs. Gather and analyse feedback to refine project objectives and deliverables. Serve as a liaison between internal teams and external partners. Prepare reports, presentations, and project documentation. Ensure adherence to regulatory and compliance requirements. Support process improvement initiatives. Assist in organising demonstrations, seminars, and engagement activities. Job Requirements: Possess a Master’s degree in Management or Engineering Experience interacting with external stakeholders for collaboration development. Industrial experience highly desirable. Experience or exposure to medical or rehabilitation technologies. Good interpersonal skills. Good communication and writing skills. Strong sense of responsibility and ownership. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified.​ Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant--Biochemistry-and-Enzyme-Engineering-_R00025610-1": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (Biochemistry and Enzyme Engineering)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJoin Our Team at the School of Biological Sciences, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore The School of Biological Sciences (SBS), part of the College of Science at Nanyang Technological University, was established in 2002 with a mission to advance excellence in biological and biomedical sciences. Our research spans diverse and impactful areas including infectious diseases, immunology, neurodegenerative disorders, telomere biology, and genome function. SBS is home to a vibrant, international community of scientific leaders, researchers, and professionals dedicated to innovation, discovery, and education. We are seeking a motivated Research Assistant to join the laboratory of Liang Zhao-Xun at SBS. The successful candidate will contribute to a research project focused on the characterization and engineering of enzyme biocatalysts. Job Description Plan and conduct biochemical experiments using appropriate experimental techniques and protocols. Perform molecular cloning and related molecular biology procedures. Contribute to experimental planning and design, including the development and optimization of experimental approaches. Analyze, interpret, and critically evaluate experimental data and results. Document and summarize experimental findings through written reports, presentations, and oral discussions. Communicate research progress and findings clearly and effectively to team members and relevant stakeholders. Requirements Bachelor’s degree in Chemistry, Biology, Biochemistry, or a related discipline. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Proficiency in biochemical assays, molecular cloning, protein expression, and protein structure–function studies. Competence in DNA and protein sequence and structural analysis, including sequence comparison, structure prediction, and molecular modeling. Ability to work independently and collaboratively as part of a multidisciplinary team. Strong organizational and time-management skills, with excellent attention to detail and the ability to manage multiple tasks effectively. The College of Science seeks a diverse and inclusive workforce and is committed to equality of opportunity. We welcome applications from all and recruit on the basis of merit, regardless of age, race, gender, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Ultrasound-_R00025609": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Ultrasound)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering (MAE) is a robust, dynamic and multi-disciplinary international research community comprising of world-class scientists and bright students. MAE prides itself in its excellent research capabilities in areas including advanced manufacturing, aerospace, biomedical, energy, industrial engineering, maritime engineering, robotics, etc. The school is equipped with state-of-the-art research infrastructure, housing a comprehensive range of cluster laboratories, test bedding facilities, research centres/institutes and corporate laboratories. Cutting-edge research in MAE addresses the immediate needs of our industries and supports the nation’s long-term development strategies. In the new era of industrial 4.0 and sustainable living, MAE is rigorous in developing new competencies to support the growth and competitiveness of our engineering sector in the global landscape. MAE has grown to be leader in Engineering Research, ranking amongst the top engineering schools in the world. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/mae/research . Key job purpose is to support a research project titled: Ultrasonic Diagnosis for cell SOH grading. Key Responsibilities: Design and carry out ultrasonic experiments and develop signal processing techniques Simulate ultrasonic wave propagation in complex materials Draft and submit technical progress reports at regular intervals Job Requirements: PhD degree in Mechanical/Electrical/Civil Engineering or equivalent Good knowledge of ultrasonic NDT/SHM Good numerical simulation skills Good programming skills (Matlab, C++ or Python) We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-fellow--Maritime-Studies-_R00025613-1": {
      "title": "Research fellow (Maritime Studies)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe school of Civil and Environmental Engineering (CEE) is looking for a motivated research fellow holding a PhD degree specializing in maritime studies, transportation/logistics, operations research, computer science, or a related field. The appointment is typically for one year and may be extended, subjected to performance and availability of research funding. Key Responsibilities : Conduct research on shipping and port operational optimization, maritime decarbonization, data analytics, and the development and application of novel methodologies (including LLM-based prediction and optimization) Coordinate the preparation of project reports and deliverables Publish research findings in top peer-reviewed journals and conference proceedings Collaborate with other researchers on project discussions and joint deliverables Support the preparation of research proposals and grant applications Job Requirements: A PhD degree in transport engineering, maritime transport and management, computer science, operations research, or a related field from a recognised university Strong expertise in applying large language models (LLMs) and AI techniques to prediction and optimization problems; familiarity with optimization algorithms is highly desirable Excellent programming skills in Python, C++, Java, Julia, or other relevant languages Knowledge of maritime decarbonization and alternative fuels is a plus A good record of publications in reputable peer-reviewed journals in maritime transport, logistics management, machine learning, deep learning, or optimization P roficient in both written and spoken communication Strong interpersonal skills, with the ability to work independently and deliver solutions under tight timelines Experience in proposal writing and funding application We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Executive--Finance-Department---NIE-_R00024025": {
      "title": "Executive (Finance Department) [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nABOUT THE NATIONAL INSTITUTE OF EDUCATION (NIE) The National Institute of Education (NIE), Singapore, is Singapore’s national teacher education institute and we are proud to be an integral part of the nation’s education service. We play a key role in the preparation of teachers and in the provision of teacher professional and school leadership development programmes. We are committed to our vision of being An Institute of Distinction: Leading the Future of Education and our mission to Inspire Learning, Transform Teaching and Advance Research. Read more about NIE here . NIE invites applicants to join the Finance Department as an Executive . Responsibilities You will be part of the team which handles payments and other student-related financial matters for the institute. Your responsibilities will include: Administering Financial Aid schemes, e.g. PSEA, CPF, Mendaki, Tuition Fee loan, Study loan, scholarships and bursaries. Checking that payment transactions (e.g. supplier invoices, student claims) have appropriate certification and approvals before processing payments. Handling the financial accounts, preparing GST, audit schedules and financial statements for NIE Student Union. Responding timely to enquiries pertaining to student matters. Assisting in the design, implementation and review of financial processes, policies and guidelines for continuous improvements, through streamlining and automation. Handling ad hoc duties as assigned. Requirements A Polytechnic Diploma in Accountancy or its equivalent. 2 or 3 years of working experience in accounting. Organized and meticulous in handling numbers and data. A team player with a positive working attitude and is willing to learn and adapt. Proficient in Microsoft Office applications, especially Excel pivot tables and formulas. Experience in SAP would be an added advantage. Able to adhere to timelines. Closing Date The closing date of the advertisement is 1 September 2026 . We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Other Information NIE staff can take chartered buses at their own expense from or near their homes to NIE campus.  This is subject to the availability of seats. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Lipid-or-Polymer-Formulation-_R00025603": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Lipid or Polymer Formulation)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Laboratory for RNA Delivery Therapeutics is an inter-school research laboratory across the College of Engineering and College of Science at Nanyang Technological University (NTU), focusing on the development of advanced RNA delivery technologies. The laboratory's research focuses on the design, synthesis and evaluation of novel lipid- and polymer-based delivery systems for RNA therapeutics, with particular emphasis on enhancing delivery efficiency and endosomal escape. The laboratory is led by Prof Mary Chan-Park, President's Chair Professor at NTU Singapore and Director of the Laboratory for RNA Delivery Therapeutics. The research programme includes collaborations with leading international partners to advance next-generation RNA nanomedicines. For more details, please view: https://www3.ntu.edu.sg/home/mbechan/ Key Job Purpose: We are looking for a Research Fellow to conduct research on the development of novel lipid- and polymer-based delivery systems for RNA therapeutics. The role will focus on the design, formulation and evaluation of stimuli-responsive nanoparticles to enhance RNA delivery and endosomal escape. Key Responsibilities: Develop and optimize stimuli-responsive nanoparticle formulations for RNA delivery. Formulate lipid- or polymer-based nanoparticles with RNA cargo. Characterize nanoparticle physicochemical properties and formulation performance. Evaluate RNA transfection efficiency and endosomal escape. Conduct bioimaging studies of mammalian cells and RNA delivery formulations. Perform in vivo studies using relevant animal models. Analyze and interpret experimental data, including nanoparticle and delivery performance measurements. Job Requirements: PhD in Chemistry, Chemical Engineering, Materials Science, Bioengineering, or a related discipline. Research experience in stimuli-responsive RNA delivery, lipid/polymer nanoparticle formulation, and RNA delivery evaluation. Hands-on experience in lipid or polymer formulation, bioimaging techniques (e.g. confocal microscopy, FRET, FRAP), and/or in vivo studies. Good publication record, communication skills, and ability to conduct independent research. Entry-level PhD graduates with relevant research experience are welcome to apply. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior---Cyber-Security-Governance-Specialist_R00025173": {
      "title": "Senior / Cyber Assurance & AI Security Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNTU's Centre for IT Services (CITS) manages the University's campus-wide IT infrastructure and delivers enterprise IT, learning systems and digital services that support NTU's education, research and administrative functions. As part of CITS, the Cyber Security team is responsible for strengthening the University's cybersecurity posture through Cyber Security Governance, Cyber Security Operations and Cyber Incident Management. We are seeking an experienced Senior / Cyber Assurance & AI Security Specialist to join our Cyber Security Governance team. In this role, you will play a key part in defining and governing enterprise cybersecurity frameworks, leading technical cyber assurance initiatives, and enhancing the University's resilience against evolving cyber threats. Key Responsibilities Lead technical cyber assurance initiatives by defining and governing the scope, schedules, methodologies and standards for internal and external web, mobile, network and API penetration testing. Conduct security reviews and audits of enterprise security infrastructure, maintain security documentation, and oversee complex access control administration and security-related issues. Design risk assessment frameworks and security guardrails for applications developed using AI-assisted software development platforms and establish testing methodologies to identify vulnerabilities in AI-generated code. Review and approve secure system architectures, ensuring security principles are embedded into system designs and technology implementations. Evaluate authentication solutions, network security configurations, security software updates and technical implementations to safeguard enterprise systems. Plan, manage and deliver cybersecurity risk assurance projects, ensuring project objectives, timelines, resources and budgets are effectively managed. Partner with Schools and stakeholders across the University to identify cybersecurity risks, provide expert technical consultation, and recommend appropriate risk mitigation strategies. Build trusted relationships with stakeholders by providing cybersecurity advisory services, supporting key business and technology initiatives, and promoting cybersecurity governance across the University. Requirements: Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Cyber Security or a related discipline. Professional certification in OSCP or CREST is required. Additional certifications such as CISSP, CISA, CISM or GIAC will be an advantage. At least 8 years of relevant IT experience, including at least 2 years in Cyber Security Engineering, Cyber Assurance, Penetration Testing or IT Risk and Governance. Strong knowledge of security issues in code written by AI agents (e.g., OWASP Top 10 for LLMs). Good understanding of cybersecurity frameworks and methodologies such as NIST Incident Handling Guidelines, Cyber Kill Chain, MITRE ATT&CK framework. Proficient in penetration testing methodologies, secure software development lifecycle (SSDLC), and security assessment of code repositories such as GitHub and GitLab. Demonstrated ability to perform cyber risk assessments, analyse complex technical environments, and develop effective security solutions. Proven project management capabilities with experience leading cybersecurity initiatives from planning through implementation. Excellent communication, stakeholder management and interpersonal skills, with the ability to provide expert technical consultation and influence cybersecurity outcomes across technical and business stakeholders. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/AI-Engineer--Evaluation-_R00024988": {
      "title": "AI Engineer (Evaluation)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAI Singapore (AISG) is Singapore's national programme in artificial intelligence, launched by the National Research Foundation (NRF) to anchor deep national capabilities in AI. Hosted at Nanyang Technological University (NTU), AI Singapore brings together Singapore-based research institutions and the vibrant ecosystem of AI start-ups and companies to perform use-inspired research, grow knowledge, create tools, and develop the talent to power Singapore's AI efforts. Since our inception in 2017, we have established a culture of respect, continuous learning, experimentation and curiosity, centred around innovation. The candidate will join a team of AI scientists, apprentices, data and software engineers. With the team, he or she will be responsible for building evaluations that test the limits of AI models especially in terms of its multilingual, multicultural and multimodal capabilities. Duties and Responsibilities: Develop and maintain evaluation frameworks and pipelines to measure the capabilities of Large Language Models (LLMs). Keep up to date and experiment with the latest research in multilingual, multicultural, and multimodal LLM evaluations such as the LLM-as-a-Judge paradigm. Work with partners to collect, translate and verify evaluation datasets. Perform the necessary data preparation and analysis, AI modelling, coding, testing, validation and deployment to ensure reliable and scalable AI solutions. Collaborate with cross-functional teams within AI Products to design and resolve issues. Maintain code repository and documentation standards. Contribute to community engagement activities such as sharings via technical session meet-ups and article write-ups, and participating in discussion forums. Requirements: Graduate from a degree program in computer science, AI, data science or related fields (or equivalent practical experience). Deep understanding of LLM evaluation experimental design and the advantages/limitations of various LLM evaluation methods. Experience in LLM inference frameworks such as vLLM and AI/Deep Learning frameworks such as PyTorch. Writing production level code in Python and using version control systems such as Git. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Independent learner that is capable of reading and understanding research papers. Fluent in English and one other Southeast Asian language for the purposes of understanding how to build quality evaluations from a multilingual and multicultural perspective. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive---Assistant-Manager--Industry-and-Research-Collaborations_R00024746": {
      "title": "Senior Executive / Assistant Manager, Industry and Research Collaborations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe College of Engineering (CoE) at Nanyang Technological University (NTU), Singapore invites applications for the position of Senior Executive/Assistant Manager, Industry and Research Collaborations. CoE is NTU’s largest and most research‑intensive college, comprising five internationally recognised engineering schools and sitting at the strategic core of the University’s academic mission. Working within CoE offers the opportunity to operate at College level, supporting impactful research collaborations that span disciplines, Schools, and external partners, within a collaborative and mission‑driven environment committed to research excellence and institutional impact. Role Overview As part of the College of Engineering’s Research & Partnerships Team, you will support the end‑to‑end administration of industry and research agreements that enable impactful research collaborations at NTU. Working under the guidance of senior team members, you will contribute to the accurate, timely and compliant processing of research agreements and post‑award activities. This role offers hands‑on exposure to how research collaborations are structured, reviewed, executed and supported within a leading research‑intensive university environment. Job Responsibilities: Your responsibilities will focus on agreement management execution and coordination, including: Supporting the administration of the full lifecycle of industry and research agreements (e.g. Non-Disclosure Agreements, Materials Transfer Agreements, Project Agreements, Research Collaboration Agreements, MoUs and Variation Agreements), from initiation to execution and closure Assisting with the preparation of agreement drafts using approved institutional templates and ensuring supporting documentation is complete and accurate Coordinating internal review and approval workflows with relevant offices such as Legal & Secretary Office, NTUitive and Finance, under established processes Coordinating closely across Schools, central offices, faculty, and external stakeholders to facilitate timely review, negotiation, resolution of issues, and execution of agreements Supporting the setup and maintenance of project records and post‑award information in the University’s research management systems Assisting with agreement variations, extensions and project closure processes in accordance with approved terms and guidance Maintaining tracking records and reports to monitor agreement status and pending actions Contributing to the upkeep of standard operating procedures, checklists and process documentation related to agreement handling Any other ad-hoc initiatives and assignments undertaken by the Office Requirements: Bachelor's degree in any discipline. Degree in engineering, business, law, public policy, administration or related fields will be advantageous. Entry-level candidates with a strong interest in research administration, contracts or higher‑education research environments are welcome to apply Prior exposure to research administration, agreements, grants, contracts or compliance‑related work will be an advantage but is not required Strong organisational skills with the ability to manage multiple tasks and follow structured processes Good written and verbal communication skills, with attention to clarity, accuracy and professionalism Attention to detail and willingness to learn institutional policies, systems and workflows IT‑savvy, with working knowledge of Microsoft Office applications We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Student-Administration_R00024595": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Student Administration",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nYoung and research-intensive, Nanyang Technological University, Singapore (NTU Singapore) is ranked among the world’s top universities. NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science (CCDS) is a leading college that is known for its excellent curriculum, outstanding and impactful research, and world-renowned faculty. A hotbed of cutting-edge technology and groundbreaking research, the College aims to groom the next generation of leaders, thinkers, and innovators to thrive in the digital age. Located in the heart of Asia, NTU’s College of Computing and Data Science is an ‘exciting place to learn and grow'. We welcome you to join our community of faculty, students and alumni who are shaping the future of AI, Data Science and Computing.  The incumbent will support the day-to-day administration and coordination of postgraduate academic and research-related matters, including admissions, course registration, examinations, curriculum and syllabus review, student records management, student enquiries, and policy documentation. The incumbent will work closely with academic leaders, university stakeholders, and students to ensure the efficient delivery of services and the smooth operation of Graduate Studies functions. Job Responsibilities: Support the full spectrum of postgraduate student administration, including admissions, course registration, course exemptions, briefings, examinations, leave matters, outreach and publicity, website content maintenance, overseas conference processing, research internship programmes, and related operational processes. Partner with Associate Deans, Programme Directors, and academic staff to review curricula and syllabi, and to prepare, coordinate, and submit academic proposals, changes, and related documentation. Plan, coordinate, and oversee the end-to-end examination process, including examination timetable preparation, venue coordination, examination administration, result processing support, and post-examination follow-up. Prepare, update, and maintain student handbooks, FAQs, student instructions, policy documents, workflow guides, letters, timelines, checklists, forms, and other operational materials to ensure accuracy and consistency. Administer SkillsFuture claims and other initiatives managed by the Centre for Professional and Continuing Education (PACE), ensuring compliance with relevant policies and submission requirements. Serve as a main point of contact for Master of Science programme enquiries via counter, email, and phone, and provide timely and professional support to students, alumni, faculty, and external stakeholders. Support the management of research integrity matters, including coordination of related cases, documentation, tracking, and administrative follow-up. Provide student advisory support on general academic and administrative matters and refer cases requiring escalation or specialist intervention as appropriate. Liaise closely with NTU offices, departments, and other schools to coordinate postgraduate academic matters and ensure smooth cross-functional operations. Maintain accurate and timely updates of graduate student records and programme data in college and university systems, ensuring data integrity and compliance with internal requirements. Support the Manager/Assistant Director across all areas of Research and Graduate Studies, including data collation, statistical reporting, presentation materials, ad hoc seminars, events, and other assigned projects. Evaluate existing workflows and implement improvements to enhance efficiency, accuracy, and responsiveness. Job Requirements : A degree with at least 3 years of relevant experience, preferably in an educational institution or higher education environment. Prior experience in student administration, postgraduate programme operations, or academic support is highly preferred. Strong proficiency in Microsoft Office applications and office IT systems; comfortable working with data, databases, and online administrative platforms. Strong system and data literacy, with the ability to handle large volumes of information accurately and efficiently. Meticulous, well-organised, and detail-oriented, with a strong sense of ownership and follow-through. Service-oriented with excellent interpersonal, communication, and organisational skills. Able to engage effectively with stakeholders at different levels, including students, faculty, and administrative colleagues. Able to multitask, manage competing deadlines, and work under pressure with minimal supervision. Strong analytical, problem-solving, and coordination skills, with the ability to work both independently and collaboratively. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Administrative-Support_R00025611": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Administrative Support",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nWe are seeking an experienced administrative professional to take on a senior role providing strategic and operational support across procurement and grants administration for the Earth Observatory of Singapore (EOS) and the Asian School of the Environment (ASE). As EOS and ASE research activities are closely integrated, this role extends support across both units to ensure smooth coordination, financial stewardship, and policy compliance. In this role, you will act as the primary subject-matter expert and advisor on procurement and grants administration, independently managing end-to-end workflows and advising Principal Investigators and researchers on funding compliance. You will take ownership of grant financial management — including budget monitoring, virement submissions, and grant claims for key research projects such as the seismic project — while also managing the engagement of external professionals for fieldwork and the design of costing and charging frameworks. Working closely with internal and external stakeholders, you will provide senior-level administrative and operational support for research-related activities and organisational initiatives within EOS & ASE. Job Responsibilities Serve as the primary subject-matter expert and first point of contact for all procurement matters across ASE and EOS, providing strategic advisory and independently managing end-to-end Ariba procurement processes including SVP, ITQ, ITT, Online Payment, Advance Payment, and Cash Advance, in compliance with University guidelines. Advise on Advance Payment requests and Cash Advance applications under exceptional circumstances, proactively guiding requestors toward more efficient and compliant alternatives. Provide senior-level procurement advisory and administrative support to ASE/EOS stakeholders, including procurement of research equipment, consumables, software and services, ensuring alignment with Delegation of Authority (DOA) and grant funding terms. Monitor grant budgets and expenditures, prepare financial reports, and process grant virements, ensuring expenditure remains aligned with approved budgets and funding agency guidelines. Manage the submission of grant claims, including but not limited for the seismic project, ensuring timely, accurate, and compliant reporting to funding agencies. Keep abreast of university procurement and grant policy updates, and proactively communicate implications to internal stakeholders. Provide strategic guidance to research clusters (e.g. Centre of Geohazards Operation (CGO), Remote Sensing (RS), seismic project on fieldwork-related matters, including the engagement of external professionals through Contract for Service (CFS) or Research Consultancy Agreement (RCA). Lead and oversee logistics for open houses and workshops across researcher clusters, including but not limited to CGO and RS. Drive the design and development of costing and charging frameworks, including CGO, EOS-RS, and other applicable units, by establishing standardised cost models for fieldwork activities, projects, and related services.Conduct benchmarking and market analysis of pricing and costing models used by industry partners, companies, and peer universities to enhance and optimise charging strategies. Perform any other duties as assigned to support the team’s and school/research center’s objectives. Job Requirements Bachelor’s degree in Business Management, Finance, or a related field. At least 4-6 years of relevant experience in administrative, procurement, or grants/financial administration, preferably in a university or research environment, with demonstrated ability to operate independently at a senior level. Strong understanding of procurement processes and grant/financial administration, with extensive working knowledge of ARIBA/SAP. Proven experience in grant management, including budget monitoring, virement processing, and grant claims submission. Strong proficiency in Microsoft applications, including Word, Excel and PowerPoint. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with strong stakeholder management, advisory capability, and a service-oriented mindset. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple priorities independently, exercising sound judgement on both operational and strategic matters. Meticulous, with strong analytical, problem-solving, and organisational skills. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Assessment-Operations-and-Partnerships_R00025606": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Assessment Operations and Partnerships",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Office of Academic Services (OAS) plays a vital role in enabling student success across the entire academic journey by implementing and administering academic policies established by the University's academic bodies. OAS delivers comprehensive academic services from matriculation to graduation, empowering students, upholding excellence, and partnering stakeholders to provide a seamless, student-centred experience while maintaining the highest standards of integrity, governance, and professionalism. Within OAS, the Examinations team is responsible for the planning, administration, and continuous enhancement of the University's assessment ecosystem. The team ensures that assessments are conducted securely, fairly, and efficiently while safeguarding academic standards and upholding the principles of academic integrity. As the University expands its digital assessment capabilities, the team also plays a key role in supporting digital transformation initiatives and driving the adoption of technology-enabled assessment practices. Key Responsibilities: Assessment Operations: Plan and administer centralised and decentralised assessments in compliance with University assessment regulations, policies, and procedures. This includes the delivery of large-scale face-to-face centralised assessments, assessment scheduling, venue allocation, seating arrangements, logistics coordination, invigilator deployment, assessment material management, and the administration of assessment-related student cases such as medical certificate submissions and special consideration requests. Digital Assessment Operations & Adoption: Oversee the operations, readiness, and utilisation of the University's digital assessment halls, ensuring seamless assessment delivery, efficient turnaround between bookings, and consistently high facility utilisation. Partner with Schools and faculty members to support the implementation and adoption of digital assessment practices by providing operational guidance, assessment planning support, and expertise on assessment technologies and processes. Assessment Partnerships, Engagement & Service Delivery: Build trusted partnerships with stakeholders to coordinate examination operations, address operational issues and identify emerging requirements. Design and deliver engagement, communications, and outreach initiatives that strengthen stakeholder understanding, readiness, and confidence in digital assessment. Governance, Risk Management & Continuous Improvement: Support academic integrity initiatives and drive process improvements, automation, and digital transformation efforts to improve efficiency, service quality, and user experience. Resource Management & Projects: Manage procurement and vendor coordination activities and analyse operational data and performance indicators to support informed decision-making. Participate in and support cross-functional projects and institutional initiatives related to digital transformation, stakeholder engagement, and service excellence initiatives that advance OAS' strategic and operational objectives. Support administrative and governance processes to support organisational planning, financial stewardship, compliance, and operational effectiveness within OAS. Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in Business Administration, Information Systems, Data Analytics, Education, or a related field. Experience in examination administration, assessment operations, digital assessments, event management, communications, customer experience, service design or large-scale operational environments. Experience supporting high-stakes, mission-critical operations involving multiple stakeholders, competing priorities, and tight timelines will be highly advantageous. At least 3 years of relevant working experience, preferably in academic services within a higher education institution.  Demonstrated ability to manage multiple stakeholders and coordinate complex operational activities under tight timelines. Strong analytical, problem-solving, and organisational skills with the ability to interpret data and recommend process improvements. Proficient in Microsoft Office applications, particularly Excel, Word, PowerPoint, and data management tools. Meticulous, proactive, and able to work effectively in a fast-paced environment with competing priorities. Results oriented and accountable, focused on achieving outcomes that meet business needs and stakeholder expectations. Proactive and improvement minded, taking initiative to identify issues early and drive continuous enhancement of processes and systems. Adaptable, organised, and resilient, able to manage multiple tasks, stay calm under pressure, and approach problems in a structured and analytical way. Demonstrates high integrity, professionalism, and a commitment to upholding governance, service excellence, and academic integrity.  We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Engagement-Manager--AISG_R00025607": {
      "title": "Engagement Manager, AISG",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAI Singapore (AISG) is a national AI programme launched by the National Research Foundation (NRF), Singapore, to build and anchor deep national capabilities in AI. AISG is supported through a government-wide partnership including the NRF, Ministry of Digital Development and Information (MDDI), Infocomm Media Development Authority (IMDA), Economic Development Board (EDB) and Enterprise Singapore (ESG). We bring together research institutions and the vibrant ecosystem of AI start-ups and companies to support impactful research, develop talent, and power Singapore's AI efforts. ​This position will be hosted at the Nanyang Technological University (NTU) under VP (Artificial Intelligence & Digital Economy)’s office and we welcome you to join our community. We are looking for an Engagement Manager to join the Data Platform team within AI Products at AISG. The team runs a data platform which supports a global effort to collect multimodal language and cultural data — cataloguing the datasets that help AI understand the world’s underrepresented languages, and bringing together linguists, researchers, contributors, and partner organisations across Asia and beyond. This is a self-directed role focused on growing and sustaining that community and on helping to grow the data that powers the platform. Your primary mandate is outreach, growth, and data acquisition — attracting new users, contributors, and traffic to the platform, encouraging and facilitating data contributions, and keeping the community engaged and invested over time. Working towards goals and guardrails agreed with the team, you will exercise your own judgement on where and how to reach each community, whether online, in person, or through partners. You will draw on the team’s partner ecosystem as a primary means of extending reach and shape the community’s direction with a considerable degree of autonomy. This role is offered on a part-time basis and is suitable for candidates seeking flexible working arrangements. Duties and Responsibilities: Outreach and growth Attract new users, contributors, and traffic to the platform — identifying and reaching researchers, linguists, developers, and underrepresented-language communities in the venues where they already gather, from research networks and developer platforms to regional AI groups and social channels. Conceive and deliver outreach campaigns and initiatives that raise awareness of the platform, its datasets, and the opportunities to contribute. Data acquisition and contributor facilitation Serve as the first point of contact for prospective data contributors — welcoming interest and connecting willing contributors with the team. Act as the bridge between prospective contributors and the team — clarifying what contributing involves and coordinating a smooth handover for the technical process. Community engagement and retention Sustain an active, returning community — encouraging repeat contributions, supporting established contributors, and cultivating first-time visitors into lasting participants. Foster constructive conversation and support across online forums and communities and respond thoughtfully to the needs of contributors and users. Partnerships and ecosystem Cultivate relationships with the team’s research and community partners across the region and work through them to extend the platform’s reach into their audiences. Represent the platform with credibility before academic, research and community stakeholders, both online and at events where appropriate. Content, communication and measurement Develop and distribute compelling content — post, updates and materials — that stimulate participation and advocate the platform’s mission and value. Monitor engagement and growth signals — new users, contributions, platform usage, referral traffic and community activity — and refine your approach considering what works. Qualifications: You should be an accomplished community builder who works with autonomy, moves fluidly between online, in-person, and partner-led channels, and represents a research-focused, mission-driven platform with credibility before technical and non-technical audiences alike. Our ideal candidate would have: A degree in communications, marketing, public relations, the social sciences, or a related field — or equivalent professional experience. Minimum 7 years of experience in community engagement, community management, developer relations, or outreach, with a demonstrable record of growing and sustaining an active community. Proven strength in stakeholder and partnership management — establishing and sustaining productive relationships with external partners, community organisations, and other stakeholders. The ability to engage prospective data contributors — understanding their needs at a high level, explaining what contributing involves, and coordinating a smooth handover to the team. Excellent written and verbal communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to build relationships and engage audiences across cultures and time zones. The judgement to select and run the right mix of channels — online (forums, social, newsletters), in person (meetups, events), and through partners — and to plan and deliver events, programmes, and campaigns. A sound grasp of engagement metrics, with the ability to track growth and activity and adapt your approach accordingly. A high degree of self-direction: resourceful, proactive, and able to set your own rhythm and exercise sound judgement amid ambiguity with light oversight. Bonus: experience within a technology, research, or academic ecosystem; familiarity with underrepresented-language, open-data, or open-source communities; relevant regional-language ability; or experience operating within Singapore public sector or research programmes. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Analyst-Programmer--Digital-Solutions-Department---NIE-_R00025587-1": {
      "title": "Analyst Programmer (Digital Solutions Department) [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nABOUT THE NATIONAL INSTITUTE OF EDUCATION (NIE) The National Institute of Education (NIE), Singapore , is Singapore’s national teacher education institute and we are proud to be an integral part of the nation’s education service. We play a key role in the preparation of teachers and in the provision of teacher professional and school leadership development programmes. We are committed to our vision of being An Institute of Distinction: Leading the Future of Education and our mission to Inspire Learning, Transform Teaching and Advance Research . Read more about NIE here . The National Institute of Education (NIE) invites suitable candidates to join the Division of Academic Computing & Information Services (ACIS) as an Analyst Programmer (25-month contract). Key Responsibilities Design, develop, test, and implement application systems based on user requirements and project timelines. Find opportunities to design and implement AI-driven features that enhance and personalize the student digital experience. Explore and propose innovative ways to modernize student information systems by leveraging the latest technology stacks and AI-assisted development methodologies. Maintain and enhance existing in-house applications to ensure optimal performance and user experience. Collaborate with cross-functional IT teams for system deployment and integration. Ensure high standards of code quality, test coverage, and participate actively in code reviews. Troubleshoot, debug, and upgrade applications as needed. Independently manage IT projects from initiation to completion. Ensure compliance with regards to Data Governance, IT Audit, and Security policies and standards. Any other ad hoc duties as assigned. Requirements A University degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Software Engineering or a related discipline.   Minimum of 3 years of relevant experience in software development and IT project management. Sound understanding of student and examination-related business processes. Familiarity with the Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC) and Agile methodologies. Proficiency in .Net programming. Experience in GitHub Copilot or similar tools. Experience in system integration via APIs and database layers. Experience with relational databases and ORM frameworks (e.g. Hibernate). Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to adapt quickly to new technologies. Effective team player with a proactive attitude and the ability to meet tight deadlines. Possessing the following skillsets will give the applicant an added advantage: Jira for Project Management AI-Driven Automation Data Analytics tools such as Power BI Low-code development platforms (e.g. Power Apps) Closing Date The closing date of the advertisement is 9 September 2026 . We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified.   Other Information NIE staff can take chartered buses at their own expense from or near their home to the NIE campus. This is subject to the availability of bus routes and seats. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Manager--Accreditation-_R00025604-1": {
      "title": "Manager (Accreditation)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNanyang Technological University is a leading global university recognised for excellence in education and research. Nanyang Business School (NBS) is one of Asia’s premier business schools, committed to delivering impactful education and driving innovation in teaching and engagement. The Accreditation and Data Management Office (ADMO) at Nanyang Business School oversees AACSB and EQUIS accreditation, supports teaching and learning, and manages data for institutional and external reporting. We are seeking a Manager (Accreditations) to undertake the following responsibilities: Manage Assurance of Learning (AoL) reporting workflows for academic programmes and work with faculty in implementing e-assessment tools. Review course outlines to ensure alignment with Outcomes-Based Teaching and Learning (OBTL) frameworks and institutional learning goals. Manage the execution of AACSB and EQUIS accreditation processes, including coordination of timelines, milestones, deliverables and visit logistics Contribute to the development of accreditation reports and supporting documentation. Oversee data governance operations, ensuring audit readiness and compliance with institutional standards. Drive continuous improvement across key operational processes. Requirements: Must-have: Bachelor’s degree from a recognised university Minimum 8 years working experience with at least 3 years of relevant experience in accreditation, quality assurance, compliance, or related areas Strong project management and coordination skills Strong written and verbal communication skills including the ability to frame narratives and develop clear, concise, and well‑structured reports. Ability to analyse and interpret large datasets to draw meaningful insights Meticulous, with a high level of accuracy and attention to detail. Ability to engage, influence, and build effective working relationships across a wide range of stakeholders, including academic, administrative, and external partners. Strong IT skills, including proficiency in MS Office and use of AI tools to enhance productivity and work processes. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a team, with a flexible approach and the capacity to learn and adapt to new areas quickly. Resourceful and creative in problem-solving. Good to have: Experience with academic accreditation frameworks (e.g. AACSB, EQUIS or similar) Familiarity with curriculum and assessment design Experience working in a higher education environment We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/ICT-Support-Engineer--Service-Management-Department---NIE-_R00025588": {
      "title": "ICT Support Engineer (Service Management Department) [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nABOUT THE NATIONAL INSTITUTE OF EDUCATION (NIE) The National Institute of Education (NIE), Singapore is Singapore’s national teacher training institute. We are committed to our vision of being An Institute of Distinction: Leading the Future of Education , and our mission to Inspire Learning, Transform Teaching and Advance Research . Read more about NIE here . The Academic Computing and Information Services (ACIS) division oversees NIE’s ICT needs. We invite applications for the position of ICT Support Engineer to support our efforts in transforming the education landscape in Singapore. Job Summary The ICT Support Engineer supports the IT Service Operations Manager in delivering ICT support to NIE stakeholders. The role diagnoses and resolves hardware, software and service issues, identifies root causes, and escalates to external vendors when required. The engineer also uses AI-driven diagnostic tools and ITSM platforms to improve resolution efficiency. The role maintains knowledge of ICT infrastructure and works with service desk staff, technical teams, end users, and project managers to ensure smooth operations and a positive user experience. Job Responsibilities 1. End-User Support and Service Delivery Act as the first point of contact for IT and AV issues and service requests, including monitoring and escalating AI service desk chatbot inquiries. Analyse and troubleshoot incidents and perform corrective and preventive maintenance. Provide IT/AV support for events, meetings, video conferences and lessons, including after-hours support when required. Deliver IT/AV services that meet user needs and satisfaction. Track task completion and ensure adherence to service level agreements (SLAs). 2. IT/AV Systems Maintenance and Operations Perform preventive and corrective maintenance of IT/AV systems in lecture theatres, classrooms, tutorial rooms, labs and meeting rooms. Assist in the evaluation, procurement and deployment of IT/AV equipment and solutions, including AI-enhanced hardware such as intelligent auto-framing cameras and AI noise-cancellation audio systems. Participate in IT/AV projects and initiatives to improve service efficiency and user experience. 3. Documentation and Knowledge Management Document incident resolutions, best practices and standard procedures in the internal Knowledge Base. Maintain technical documentation for IT/AV configurations and deployment guides, using generative AI tools where applicable. 4. Asset and Inventory Management Maintain IT/AV asset records and update asset databases. Conduct physical asset verification and report findings for audit reconciliation and compliance. 5. Security and Compliance Collaborate with the cybersecurity team to enhance endpoint security using AI-driven threat detection and endpoint response (EDR) systems. Ensure compliance with NIE IT security policies, relevant regulatory requirements and acceptable AI usage policies. 6. Business Continuity and Process Improvement Participate in IT Business Continuity and Disaster Recovery (BCDR) programmes. Contribute to service improvement through innovation, feedback and cross-functional projects. Identify opportunities to automate routine support tasks using AI, scripts and robotic process automation (RPA). Requirements 1. Educational Background and Certifications A Polytechnic Diploma in Information & Communication Technology (ICT) or a related field, with strong knowledge of technology and systems supporting IT and AV infrastructure. ITIL Foundation certification and experience with ITIL best practices are preferred. 2. Experience and Technical Skills At least 2 years of experience in ICT support, with a proven track record in customer service and technical support. Familiarity with Generative AI assistants such as Microsoft Copilot and ChatGPT for troubleshooting, scripting and workflow automation. Solid knowledge of computer troubleshooting, networking, applications and operating systems, including Microsoft Windows, Microsoft Office, Macintosh OS and mobile devices. Knowledge of networking protocols and common software tools. Familiarity with audio/video equipment, including AV troubleshooting and setup for events, lessons and meetings. Ability to diagnose and resolve technical issues independently with minimal supervision. 3. Key Personal Attributes Proactive, self-motivated and resilient, with a strong sense of urgency and ability to work under pressure. Result-oriented and responsible, with the ability to meet deadlines and deliver work to a high standard. Collaborative team player with creativity, resourcefulness and strong problem-solving skills. Excellent written and verbal communication and interpersonal skills. 4. Innovation and Continuous Improvement Strong interest in new technologies, particularly AI and automation tools, to improve productivity and service efficiency. Ability to stay current with relevant technology trends and tools. Ability to collaborate with peers and technical teams across the organisation to resolve issues and implement solutions. Closing Date The closing date of the advertisement is 8 September 2026 . We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified.   Other Information NIE staff can take chartered buses at their own expense from or near their home to the NIE campus. This is subject to the availability of bus routes and seats. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Electrolyte-and-materials-interfaces-for-batteries-_R00025600": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Electrolyte and materials interfaces for batteries)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAt EI2 Lab www.wrzhanglab.com , we focus on advancing electrochemistry, materials, and engineering as an integrated platform to build technologies for a sustainable and resilient future. We focus on the ion conductor and its interface with other materials. We aim to understand the ion/electron transportation in the conductor, and the chemo-electro-mechanics behavior at these materials interface. By understanding and ultimately controlling these interfaces, we will enable the development of advanced energy systems and electronic devices, including high energy Li/Na batteries, all-solid-state batteries, sensors, switch, electrochemical transistors, with scalable architectures for real-world applications. The School of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research.  With over 3,000 undergraduates students and 1,000 graduate students it is one of the largest EEE schools in the world and ranks 10th in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2024 QS World University Rankings by Subjects. Today, the School has become one of the world’s largest engineering schools that nurtures competent engineers and researchers. Each year, the School graduates over a thousand students who are ready to take on great ambitions and challenges. For more details, please view: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee We are looking for a highly motivated Research Fellow to drive independent research in next-generation electrochemical energy systems ; support interdisciplinary collaborations across materials science, electrochemistry, and mechanics; mentor graduate and undergraduate students in the lab. The role will contribute to cutting-edge research in electrochemical energy storage and conversion , with a focus on solid-state batteries, interfacial chemistry, electro-chemo-mechanics, and novel energy materials. Key Responsibilities: Conduct advanced research on solid-state batteries ; high energy batteries; materials synthesis; Design and perform electrochemical, mechanical, and advanced materials characterizations. Collaborate with internal and external academic/industrial partners on joint projects. Prepare manuscripts for high-impact journal publications and present at international conferences. Contribute to grant proposal writing and new project development. Mentor and supervise PhD, Master’s, and undergraduate students in the laboratory. Job Requirements: PhD degree in Materials Science, Chemistry, Chemical Engineering, Electrical and Electronic Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, or related field At least 3 years of relevant experience in a similar role / technical hands-on experience in materials synthesis, electrochemical testing, and advanced characterization techniques. Proven track record of high-quality research publications in high-impact journals. Translation experience is very preferable. Good written and oral communication skills Ability to work independently and collaboratively in an interdisciplinary team. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Student-Life--Graduate-Studies---Programme-Management-and-Operations_R00025500-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Student Life, Graduate Studies - Programme Management and Operations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNanyang Technological University is a leading global university recognised for excellence in education and research. Nanyang Business School (NBS) is one of Asia’s premier business schools, committed to delivering impactful education and driving innovation in teaching and engagement. Working at Nanyang Technological University offers candidates the opportunity to be part of one of Asia’s leading universities with a strong global reputation in education, research, and innovation. Employees are exposed to a dynamic and international environment, working with diverse students, faculty, industry partners, and stakeholders from around the world. For programme administration and student engagement roles, NTU provides meaningful opportunities to contribute directly to student development, learning experiences, and high-impact university initiatives. The role also offers broad exposure to academic operations, event management, stakeholder engagement, and cross-functional collaboration within a fast-paced and professional environment. The incumbent will support the administration and operations of the Master of Business Administration and Specialised Masters programme, including academic administration, student engagement activities, events management, and stakeholder coordination. The role involves working closely with faculty, students, alumni, vendors, and internal departments to ensure smooth programme delivery and a positive student experience. Key responsibilities include: Manage administrative, operational, and logistics matters for student activities, programme events, and engagements. Coordinate programme-related events, including venue setup, catering, transportation, registration, and onsite support. Respond to student-related enquiries in a timely and professional manner. Support day-to-day programme administration and operations. Provide faculty and instructor support, including appointments, approvals, agreements, payments, classroom arrangements, and teaching-related requests. Support timetabling, course administration, examinations, and related academic operations. Process student reimbursements, monitor student activities budgets, and prepare budget utilisation reports. Compile, collate, and maintain accurate data, records, statistics, and reports for management reporting and audit purposes. Liaise and coordinate with students, faculty, alumni, vendors, and internal departments to ensure smooth operations and follow-through. Procure operational and event-related logistics and services in accordance with university procedures. Support other programme-related projects, operational duties, and administrative tasks as assigned. Requirements: Bachelor’s degree with at least 3 years of relevant working experience, preferably in student administration, programme management, or event management within a higher education institution. Strong organisational, coordination, and administrative skills with attention to detail. Good understanding of event planning, operational logistics, and programme administration. Customer service-oriented with strong interpersonal and stakeholder management skills. Meticulous, systematic, and able to manage multiple priorities effectively in a fast-paced environment. Proactive, resourceful, adaptable, and able to work independently with minimal supervision. Strong planning, multitasking, project coordination, and problem-solving skills, with the ability to exercise sound judgement during unexpected situations or operational challenges. Good team player with a strong sense of responsibility and ownership. Proficient in Microsoft Office applications (Excel, PowerPoint, Word, Outlook, Teams, Canva). Good written and verbal communication skills to communicate effectively with stakeholders. Strong interpersonal and stakeholder engagement skills and comfortable engaging with diverse stakeholders. Willing to support occasional evening and weekend activities when required. Willing to travel overseas with students for up to one week annually.   We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Scientist---Fellow--Fibre-Optics-_R00025599": {
      "title": "Research Scientist / Fellow (Fibre Optics)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research. With over 3,000 undergraduates students and 2,000 graduate students it is one of the largest EEE schools in the world and ranks 4th in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2025 QS World University Rankings by Subjects. Today, the School has become one of the world’s largest engineering schools that nurtures competent engineers and researchers. Each year, the School graduates over a thousand students who are ready to take on great ambitions and challenges. For more details, please view: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee We are looking for a highly motivated and skilled Research Scientist /Research Fellow to join our cutting-edge fiber optics team. The role will focus on developing next-generation high-power fiber beam combiners. The successful candidate will be responsible for developing advanced modeling and simulation (M&S) tools and the establishment of comprehensive diagnostic and characterization tools. This position requires a strong background in optical physics and hands-on experience in both computational modeling and experimental characterization of optical components. Key Responsibilities: 1. Modelling & Simulation (M&S) Tool Development Develop and customize simulation templates using Beam Propagation Method (BPM) software (e.g., BeamProp) to model optical behavior in fiber combiners, focusing on critical areas like taper transitions and fusion zones. Utilize Finite Element Method (FEM) software (e.g., COMSOL) to perform thermal analysis, modeling heat distribution and dissipation in high-power operational conditions. Define theoretical performance benchmarks for optical characteristics such as insertion loss and beam quality by integrating real-world data, such as empirical beam profiles from high-power laser diodes. Validate simulation models by calibrating them against established literature and comparing them with empirical data from fabricated components. Collaborate with the fabrication team to diagnose sub-optimal performance by identifying discrepancies between theoretical and experimental results. 2. Diagnostic Characterisation & Validation Design, build, and maintain dedicated experimental setups for the characterization of high-power fiber optic components. Conduct precise measurements of key performance metrics, including insertion loss, beam quality (M²), and thermal performance under high-power loads (> 200 W/port). Develop and standardize testing procedures to ensure consistent and reliable data collection across multiple samples. Implement diagnostic methods, such as fiber index profiling and microscopic visual inspection, to analyze post-processing effects on signal fibers. Provide crucial feedback to the M&S and fabrication teams by supplying accurate characterization data, creating a closed-loop development cycle. Job Requirements: PhD qualification degree in Physics, Optical Engineering, Electrical Engineering or related field At least 4 years of relevant experiences / technical hands-on experience in an optics lab, including the design and construction of test benches and characterization of optical components (e.g., measuring insertion loss, beam quality). Familiarity with optical and thermal simulation software, and high-power laser systems Solid theoretical understanding of fiber optics, laser physics, and heat transfer. Good written and oral communication skills Proficiency in BPM and COMSOL is highly essential. Competent in analytical skills with the ability to bridge the gap between theoretical models and experimental results. Excellent problem-solving abilities and a methodical, data-driven approach to research. Ability to work collaboratively in a fast-paced environment. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
