    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Lead--Finance--R2R-_R00024966": {
      "title": "Lead, Finance (R2R)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 22 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNTU Shared Services (NSS) Finance delivers end-to-end finance services across the University, supporting operational excellence, governance, and strategic decision-making. The Record-to-Report (R2R) function is a core pillar responsible for financial reporting, accounting integrity, and data governance. This role leads the R2R function covering General Ledger, Fixed Assets and Master Data Management, ensuring accurate and timely financial close and reporting. The position also drives process optimisation, automation, and transformation initiatives, positioning R2R as a strategic finance partner. Success in this role will be reflected in stronger close discipline, improved reporting quality, enhanced data governance, and measurable progress in process optimisation and digitalisation across the R2R function. Why Join This Role This role offers the opportunity to shape the future of R2R within a large, complex university environment, with exposure to enterprise-wide finance transformation, digitalisation and leadership-level decision support. The role combines operational leadership with the mandate to modernise processes, strengthen data and reporting capabilities, and contribute to the next phase of finance shared services at NTU. Key Responsibilities: Lead end-to-end R2R operations, including General Ledger, Fixed Assets and Master Data Management Oversee month-end, quarter-end and year-end financial close, ensuring accuracy, completeness and strong cut-off discipline Manage balance sheet integrity, including reconciliation governance and timely resolution of exceptions Support preparation of management, statutory and audit reports, ensuring reliability and compliance Ensure compliance with accounting standards, taxation requirements (including GST and Withholding Tax reporting validation) and NTU policies Drive review and validation of GST/WHT returns, ensuring alignment with GL and underlying financial data Strengthen financial controls, governance frameworks and audit readiness across R2R processes Drive process improvements, automation and digital initiatives (e.g. RPA, analytics, system enhancements) Oversee finance system governance and data integrity, including master data quality and controls Partner stakeholders (OFIN, Schools, Departments, CITS) to provide accounting advisory and resolve complex issues Lead and develop the R2R team, building strong technical accounting, systems and data capabilities Requirements: Degree in Accountancy or equivalent (CPA/CA preferred) Minimum 10 years of relevant experience in financial reporting / GL / R2R Strong knowledge of: - Financial close and reporting - General Ledger and balance sheet governance - Fixed assets accounting - Accounting standards and GST/WHT principles Experience in leading teams and managing stakeholders Experience as a digital finance change agents on AI-enabled finance processes We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Director--Office-of-Commercial-and-Auxiliary-Services_R00024439": {
      "title": "Director, Office of Commercial and Auxiliary Services",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 22 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNTU is seeking an experienced and visionary leader to head its Office of Commercial and Auxiliary Services (OCAS). This senior leadership role is responsible for providing strategic leadership and oversight in the policies and operations relating to hospitality, commercial leasing, real estate management, and auxiliary services. In addition, the Director plays an active role and collaborates with stakeholders to cultivate a vibrant campus culture, involve both students and employees, and foster a strong sense of community. Key Responsibilities Provide strategic leadership for NTU’s hospitality, commercial leasing, real estate, and auxiliary services functions. Drive the transformation of NTU into a vibrant, welcoming, and sustainable environment for students, staff, and the wider community. Lead initiatives to enhance campus life, including F&B offerings, hospitality services, amenities, and community-facing activities. Oversee the University’s hospitality assets and ensure high standards of quality, service excellence, and financial sustainability. Provide strategic oversight of key auxiliary services such as campus transportation and car park operations, working closely with outsourced service providers. Lead the planning, development, and refurbishment of major campus hospitality and lifestyle assets. Develop and manage business strategies to optimise the use of leased assets and maximise revenue from commercial activities. Build strong partnerships with internal and external stakeholders to deliver innovative and value-driven solutions. Identify and manage strategic, financial, and operational risks across all areas under OCAS’s purview. Requirements Bachelor’s degree in Business Administration, Hospitality Management, or a related discipline; a Master’s degree is an advantage. A minimum of 18 years of demonstrated experience in commercial leasing, hospitality, events management, community engagement, or university student life, along with a successful history in developing and implementing strategic initiatives and managing large-scale projects. Proven track record in leading transformation and implementing change management. Strong strategic and commercial acumen, with experience in business planning, stakeholder management, and change leadership. Ability to operate effectively in a complex, multi-stakeholder environment. Passion for enhancing campus life and community engagement, with an inclusive and collaborative leadership style. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow---Integrated-Sensing-and-Communications--ISAC--with-Reconfigurable-Intelligent-Metasurfaces--RIS--_R00025541": {
      "title": "Research Fellow ( Integrated Sensing and Communications (ISAC) with Reconfigurable Intelligent Metasurfaces (RIS))",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 22 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research. With over 3,000 undergraduates students and 2,000 graduate students it is one of the largest EEE schools in the world and ranks 4th in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2025 QS World University Rankings by Subjects. Today, the School has become one of the world’s largest engineering schools that nurtures competent engineers and researchers. Each year, the School graduates over a thousand students who are ready to take on great ambitions and challenges. For more details, please view: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee We are looking for a Research Fellow to support the research on Integrated Sensing and Communications (ISAC) with Reconfigurable Intelligent Metasurfaces (RIS). Key Responsibilities: Design the algorithm for Integrated Sensing and Communications (ISAC). Utilizing advanced antenna techniques, e.g. Reconfigurable Intelligent Metasurfaces (RIS), or Stacked Intelligent Metasurfaces (SIM). Conduct simulation and perform experiment in some scenarios. Document research outcome to publish at top international conference / journal. Write report for the project progress. Work with other research fellow and PhD students for the system development. Job Requirements: PhD degree in Electrical and Electronic Engineering, or related field. Good publication record. Have prior experience in conducting experiments is a plus. A thorough knowledge of the ISAC, RIS is highly preferred. Excellent interpersonal communication and presentation skills We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Soundscape-Engineering-_R00025536": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Soundscape Engineering)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 22 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research. With over 3,000 undergraduates students and 2,000 graduate students it is one of the largest EEE schools in the world and ranks 4th in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2025 QS World University Rankings by Subjects. Today, the School has become one of the world’s largest engineering schools that nurtures competent engineers and researchers. Each year, the School graduates over a thousand students who are ready to take on great ambitions and challenges. For more details, please view: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee We are looking for a Research Fellow to push the development of the AIoT system, which is a key thrust in a Soundscape project. This is a big project where there is a strong emphasis in deployment, testing and scaling up in building. There are many diverse factors to come up with a robust and stable system to made it more industry ready that focus on cross-platform instead of current single platform. Furthermore, the success of this thrust will help to increase university engagement with industry that facilitate tech transfer that benefited university and industry. The role will focus on data curation, AI model training, edge-AI deployment, subjective evaluation, and AIoT implementation. Key Responsibilities: Writing, debugging, optimizing and testing of source code with an emphasis on audio applications Maintenance and improvement of existing audio algorithm code base including noise reduction, acoustic echo cancellation, automatic gain control, voice activity detection, packet loss compensation and other audio enhancements Software development of new algorithmic audio processing solutions including the existing areas mentioned above and additionally including state of the art audio codecs, audibility and intelligibility enhancements, microphone array processing, soundscape and other audio enhancements Publish journal and conference papers as dictated by the assigned projects. Provide guidance of Master/Undergraduate students Need more than 3 years of research experience working in this area. Job Requirements: PhD qualification degree in soundscape engineering and evaluation or related field At least 3 years of relevant experiences in soundscape engineering / technical hands-on experience soundscape evaluation Familiarity with soundscape ISO standards Good written and oral communication skills Proficiency in AI (python) programming and R programming Competent in designing subjective experiments and evaluation Ability to work independently, develop solutions under strict timelines, meticulous and eye for details / excellent organizational and time management skills and have experiences in publishing soundscape engineering papers, Ability to build rapport and influence stakeholders at all levels Ability to work collaboratively in a fast-paced environment. We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
