    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Engineer-I--Aerospace-Engineering---Electrical-Engineering---Computer-Science-_R00025447-1": {
      "title": "Research Engineer I (Aerospace Engineering / Electrical Engineering / Computer Science)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nUnder the Air Traffic Management Research Institute (ATMRI) (http://atmri.ntu.edu.sg/), Nanyang Technological University, you will be part of a research team to study the use of Artificial Intelligence and Data Analytics in Air Traffic Management Systems. The selected candidate will work on developing innovative machine learning models to address key challenges in the future airspace system, including traffic prediction, optimization, and safety enhancements. Key Responsibilities:   Develop and implement machine learning models for air traffic prediction, flow management, and conflict detection. Apply deep learning, reinforcement learning, and other advanced AI techniques to improve decision-making in ATM systems. Work with real-time and historical air traffic data (e.g., ADS-B) to build predictive models for air traffic demand and capacity. Collaborate with a team of researchers and engineers to integrate machine learning models into ATM decision support systems. Analyze the performance of machine learning models and optimize their scalability for real-world airspace management applications. Participate in project meetings, prepare research reports, and contribute to publications in top-tier academic conferences and journals. Assist in the preparation of project proposals and technical documentation. Job Requirements: Bachelor of Engineering degree in Aerospace Engineering//Electrical Engineering Computer Sc. Demonstrated evidence of developing Machine Learning and Optimization models for Air Traffic problems. Two years of working experience in Machine Learning and Data Science Strong programming skills in Python and Machine Learning. Good writing and communication skills. Independent and team player. We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--CLIC-_R00025445": {
      "title": "Research Associate (CLIC)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCentre for Lifelong Learning and Individualised Cognition CLIC is a research collaboration between the University of Cambridge and Nanyang Technological University (NTU) and hosted by the Cambridge Centre for Advanced Research and Education in Singapore (CARES) that aims to develop neuroscience-based interventions for lifelong flexible learning. Launched in October 2020 and funded by the National Research Foundation Singapore, CLIC brings together a multidisciplinary team of psychologists, neuroscientists, linguists and educators who conduct innovative research in the science of learning. The world of today is constantly evolving to keep pace with advances in technology and globalisation, requiring individuals to adapt and develop new skills to ensure resilience through a culture of lifelong flexible learning. Mental flexibility is required in order to adapt to change, problem-solve creatively in new situations and make the most of opportunities including emerging career opportunities. The capacity for cognitive flexibility is thus central to the modern digital age and our education system needs innovation to ensure citizens are equipped to develop these future skills. For example, major global challenges, including climate change, renewable energy, and food security, will require novel and creative approaches and solutions. CLIC researchers are developing a neuroscience-based model of flexible learning, including important social contextual factors, in order to inform the design of practical, real-life interventions for use in schools and the workplace. This will ensure that individuals are not only prepared for future career success, but also have a good quality of life and wellbeing, thus supporting a flourishing society. For more details, please view: https://www.cares.cam.ac.uk/research/clic/ We are looking for a  Research Associate to support research activities on cognitive flexibility and learning, and training-related brain changes among adults and adolescents . We anticipate the successful candidate to perform within a dynamic interdisciplinary research environment working collaboratively with project team members and take on opportunities for involvement in research activities related to science education, language and cognition, and cognition/learning and pedagogy. Key Responsibilities: Conducting literature review Conducting interviews Liaising with school personnel Survey construction, evaluation, and administration Familiarity with behavioral task data and experience in data management. Proven experience in data analysis, with proficiency in R for data wrangling and basic statistical analyses (e.g., ANOVA, regression, structural equation modelling, principal factor analysis). Understanding of online and offline psychological research tools, such as Qualtrics, Gorilla, and PsychoPy. Familiarity with standard formats for reporting data analysis, tables, figures and a solid understanding of APA 7th edition style guidelines. Strong communication skills and the ability to work efficiently. Able to collaborate well with others and deliver work on time. Assist in quantitative and qualitative processing and analysis Project and data management, maintain research records Collect primary data, responsible for data coding and entry Report preparation Assisting in the analysis of findings Other research related tasks as assigned by the Principal Investigator Job Requirements: Master’s degree in psychology with a background in cognition, education/learning, pedagogy, or related field. Experience in conducting, collecting data for and analysing surveys, psychological testing (computerised), behavioural testing and cognitive experiments Experience in conducting literature reviews and writing academic reports Experience with statistical analysis using SPSS and/or R language Good ICT skills Good communication skills and other interpersonal skills Excellent organizational skills and able to work effectively within deadlines Experience preparing reports, protocols, presentations and manuscripts with guidance Interest in research at the intersection of neuroscience, social science, education, and cognition We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Multi-Agent-Path-Planning-for-Autonomous-Drone-Operations-_R00025443": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Multi-Agent Path Planning for Autonomous Drone Operations)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering (MAE) is a robust, dynamic and multi-disciplinary international research community comprising of world-class scientists and bright students. MAE prides itself in its excellent research capabilities in areas including advanced manufacturing, aerospace, biomedical, energy, industrial engineering, maritime engineering, robotics, etc. The school is equipped with state-of-the-art research infrastructure, housing a comprehensive range of cluster laboratories, test bedding facilities, research centres/institutes and corporate laboratories. Cutting-edge research in MAE addresses the immediate needs of our industries and supports the nation’s long-term development strategies. In the new era of industrial 4.0 and sustainable living, MAE is rigorous in developing new competencies to support the growth and competitiveness of our engineering sector in the global landscape. MAE has grown to be leader in Engineering Research, ranking amongst the top engineering schools in the world. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/mae/research . We are looking for a Research Fellow in Multi-Agent Path Planning for Autonomous Drone Operations to develop learning-based model predictive control (MPC) algorithms for multi-agent multirotor drone navigation around vessels in maritime environments. The role will focus on integrating multirotor crash predictions with vessel protected volume estimates to identify safety-buffer overlaps, developing multi-agent path-planning, and machine-learning methods for corridor allocation, airspace capacity optimisation, and defining safe air corridors and operational capacity limits under varying maritime traffic conditions. Key Responsibilities: Develop multi-agent path-planning frameworks for safe and efficient multirotor operations in maritime environments. Formulate multi-agent navigation problems, including state and action representation, safety constraints, vessel-protected volumes, route allocation, and trajectory optimisation. Develop model predictive control and multi-agent model predictive control algorithms for path planning under dynamic maritime conditions. Develop capacity optimisation algorithms that enable drones to respond to vessel movements, environmental disturbances, and changes in operational constraints. Integrate drone airspace-usage prediction, vessel protected volume estimation, navigation, decision-making, and control modules within a simulation-based validation framework. Develop methods to estimate the safe operational capacity for drone operations under different vessel traffic, airspace, and environmental scenarios. Design and conduct simulation experiments, sensitivity analyses, and validation studies to evaluate navigation safety, efficiency, robustness, scalability, and generalisation. Work with PhD students, research engineers, vessel operators, drone operators, and project collaborators to support system integration, testing, validation, and demonstration. Prepare technical reports, research publications, presentations, project deliverables, and documentation for stakeholder and expert review. Job Requirements: Education qualifications PhD degree in Robotics, Aerospace Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Electrical and Electronic Engineering, Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, or a closely related discipline. Strong research background in multi-agent reinforcement learning, multi-robot systems, autonomous systems, or learning-based navigation. A strong publication record in relevant journals or conferences would be an advantage. Soft skills Strong communication and problem-solving skills. Strong sense of ownership, responsibility, and initiative. Ability to mentor junior researchers, PhD students, or research engineers and collaborate with industry partners, and project stakeholders. Willingness to support project reporting and milestone reviews. Hard skills Strong programming skills in Python and deep learning frameworks such as PyTorch or TensorFlow. Experience in autonomous navigation, path planning, trajectory optimisation, conflict detection, or collision avoidance. Experience in model predictive control and multi-agent model predictive control algorithms. Familiarity with optimisation techniques, machine-learning methods and data-driven modelling. Familiarity with robotics and autonomous-system simulation environments such as ROS/ROS2, Gazebo, AirSim, Unity, or equivalent platforms. Knowledge of vessel-motion prediction, dynamic obstacle avoidance, separation assurance, or traffic-aware navigation would be advantageous. Familiarity with geospatial data, maritime traffic data, Automatic Identification System data, or airspace-capacity modelling would be beneficial. Experience Experience in developing learning-based model predictive control algorithms in simulation. Experience in multi-agent robotic systems, drone swarms, or autonomous decision making. Experience in integrating prediction, planning, decision-making, and control modules within a simulation or experimental framework. Experience with control algorithms for embodied AI systems is desirable. Competencies Ability to formulate and solve navigation and optimisation problems under uncertainty, dynamic constraints, and changing operational conditions. Ability to work across AI, robotics, control, and UAV autonomy domains. Ability to deliver research outcomes within project timelines and contribute to high-quality publications We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Engineer--Structural-Finite-Element-Analysis-for-Maritime-Drone-Operations-_R00025441": {
      "title": "Research Engineer (Structural/Finite Element Analysis for Maritime Drone Operations)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering (MAE) is a robust, dynamic and multi-disciplinary international research community comprising of world-class scientists and bright students. MAE prides itself in its excellent research capabilities in areas including advanced manufacturing, aerospace, biomedical, energy, industrial engineering, maritime engineering, robotics, etc. The school is equipped with state-of-the-art research infrastructure, housing a comprehensive range of cluster laboratories, test bedding facilities, research centres/institutes and corporate laboratories. Cutting-edge research in MAE addresses the immediate needs of our industries and supports the nation’s long-term development strategies. In the new era of industrial 4.0 and sustainable living, MAE is rigorous in developing new competencies to support the growth and competitiveness of our engineering sector in the global landscape. MAE has grown to be leader in Engineering Research, ranking amongst the top engineering schools in the world. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/mae/research . We are looking for a Research Engineer in Structural/Finite Element Analysis for Maritime Drone Operations to investigate the risk that multirotor drone collisions pose to vessels operating in maritime environments. The role will focus on developing and executing finite element analysis (FEA) simulations of drone-vessel impacts, estimating structural damage to critical vessel subsystems, and translating simulation outputs into damage severity classifications and risk matrices that feed into the project’s separation-assurance framework and the Maritime Digital Twin. The role will also be involved in developing data-driven or physics-informed surrogate models of the FEA simulations to enable fast, generalizable damage predictions across a range of drone and vessel scenarios. Key Responsibilities: Develop finite element analysis (FEA) frameworks to estimate structural damage from multirotor drone-vessel collisions in maritime environments. Formulate impact analysis problems, including drone impact trajectories, weight classes, vessel component geometry and material properties, and structural damage severity classification. Develop and execute nonlinear/explicit dynamic FEA simulations (e.g., ANSYS, Abaqus) covering mid-flight and landing-phase crash scenarios on different vessel types. Develop methods to translate structural damage severity into functional-impact and risk classifications for critical vessel subsystems. Develop data-driven or physics-informed surrogate models trained on FEA outputs to accelerate damage-severity prediction, reducing reliance on repeated simulations. Integrate damage estimation outputs with crash-area prediction and separation-assurance models within the project’s overall risk framework and the Maritime Digital Twin. Identify and prioritise critical versus non-critical vessel components and zones, working with vessel operators and the classification society to obtain relevant structural data. Design and conduct simulation experiments, sensitivity analyses, and validation studies to evaluate damage estimation accuracy, robustness, and generalisation across vessel types. Work with PhD students, research fellows, vessel operators, drone operators, and project collaborators to support system integration, testing, validation, and demonstration. Prepare technical reports, research publications, presentations, project deliverables, and documentation for stakeholder and expert review. Job Requirements: Education qualifications Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Aerospace Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Material Science and Engineering, Civil/Structural Engineering, or a closely related discipline. Strong academic or project background in finite element analysis, structural mechanics, or impact/crash simulation. Research or project experience in maritime/naval structures, impact studies, or structural damage assessment would be advantageous. Soft skills Strong communication and problem-solving skills. Strong sense of ownership, responsibility, and initiative. Ability to work effectively with researchers, engineers, students, industry partners, and project stakeholders. Willingness to support project reporting and milestone reviews. Hard skills Demonstrated hands-on experience with FEA software, specifically nonlinear or explicit dynamic solvers used for impact/crash simulation (e.g., Abaqus Explicit, LS-DYNA, or ANSYS Explicit Dynamics). Competent in structural mechanics, material behaviour under dynamic/impact loading, and failure/damage modelling. Familiarity with drone dynamics or aerospace impact studies would be advantageous. Scripting ability (e.g., Python) for simulation automation, post-processing, or coupling FEA outputs with downstream risk models. Experience translating engineering simulation results into risk matrices or decision-support outputs for non-specialist stakeholders would be beneficial. Programming skills in Python or MATLAB for simulation data processing and analysis would be an advantage. Familiarity with surrogate modelling and physics-informed neural networks (PINNs) for generalising simulation-based predictions would be an advantage. Experience Experience integrating simulation, damage/risk assessment, and reporting workflows within a research or engineering project framework. Competencies Ability to scope, build, and validate simulation models independently from limited or partial input data. Ability to work across structural engineering, impact mechanics, and maritime domains. Ability to deliver research outcomes within project timelines and contribute to high-quality publications. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Manager--Digital-Optimisation_R00025442": {
      "title": "Manager, Digital Optimisation",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Manager, Digital Optimization plays a strategic role in driving digital transformation, process innovation, data-driven decision-making, and AI adoption within the Office of Campus Housing (OCH). This role is responsible for leading the optimization and continuous enhancement of the Housing Management System (HMS) and related digital platforms to support efficient, scalable, and user-centric housing operations. We are seeking a highly motivated and forward-thinking professional to manage, support and enhance HMS and other IT systems while spearheading initiatives in automation, analytics, Generative AI and Agentic AI to improve operational efficiency and service delivery. The successful candidate should possess strong analytical, organizational, and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to translate business needs into practical digital solutions and work efficiently with internal stakeholders, IT teams and external vendors. Duties & Responsibilities: Lead stakeholder engagement and change management prior to rollout of new features and functionalities. Provide strategic oversight of the HMS ensuring that the platform effectively supports end-to-end housing operations.  Oversee the governance and accuracy for updating of housing-related digital content across NTU’s website and Student’s intranet. Support data analysis and statistical reports required by stakeholders. This includes analyses on applications, occupancy rates, check-in/out data, withdrawal, and other relevant metrics that provide insights into the efficiency of operations and outreach to applicants or residents. Provide effective user support structure where users’ inquiries / issues are addressed effectively and making sure that user guide is developed and updated for HMS. Manage vendor relationships and service delivery performance, working closely with external partners and internal stakeholders to resolve system issues, implement enhancements, and ensure operational reliability. Self-motivated and work independently for ad-hoc projects when assigned. Lead the analysis of data to derive insights for informed decision-making. Champion Business Process Re-engineering (BPR) to optimise productivity and satisfaction. Leverage data analytics, automation technologies, Generative AI, and Agentic AI solutions to identify opportunities for operational improvement, process optimization, and enhanced decision-making. Evaluate emerging technologies, including Generative AI, Agentic AI, Machine Learning, Robotic Process Automation (RPA), and digital productivity tools, and translate them into practical business solutions. Promote a culture of innovation, continuous improvement, and data-driven decision-making through the adoption of digital technologies and AI-enabled solutions. Requirements: Degree or and Diploma holders in Information Systems, Computer Science, Data Science, Artificial Intelligence, Engineering, or a related discipline. Minimum 8 to 10 years of relevant working experience with Operations, Finance, Human Resources and IT and at least 2 years in managerial role. Demonstrates excellent skills in teamwork and collaboration. Organized and able to work well under pressure and with tight deadlines. Knowledge of Generative AI technologies, including prompt engineering, retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), AI copilots, and knowledge management solutions. Understanding of Agentic AI concepts, autonomous agents, workflow orchestration, AI-assisted decision support, and multi-agent systems. Experience in applying AI and automation technologies to improve business processes, service delivery and operational efficiency. Strong knowledge of Excel functions, Excel Power Query, Pivot and SQL. Familiar and hands-on with Robotic Process Automation software. Proficiency in data analysis and deriving actionable insights. Prior experience in hostel management and/or IT support role will be an added advantage. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant-Associate--AI-in-Medicine_R00025439-1": {
      "title": "Research Assistant/Associate, AI in Medicine",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCentre of AI in Medicine is a university-level research centre with the mission to bridge the gap between cutting-edge Artificial Intelligence (AI) technologies and practical applications in healthcare, The key objective is to spearheadresearch and development to revolutionise patient care and inform public health policies. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/c-aim We are seeking a Research Assistant / Research Associate to contribute towards the daily operational needs and strategic research priorities of the NTU Centre of AI in Medicine (C-AIM). The role will support the smooth running of C-AIM’s infrastructure, AVIT systems, administrative processes, procurement, audits, documentation, and coordination activities, ensuring that the Centre’s day-to-day functions are reliable, efficient, and responsive to project and stakeholder needs. In parallel, the candidate will provide behavioral, communications and social science research support for strategic healthcare AI implementation projects, including human-machine interactions, outcomes-based evidence, survey design and rollout, cohort recruitment, conversational analysis, simulation- and observation-based studies, data preparation, processing and analysis, project documentation, grant and proposal support, and coordination with internal and external collaborators. Through this dual operational and research-facing role, the candidate will help C-AIM translate AI innovations into practical healthcare applications that advance patient care, health system improvement, and responsible AI implementation in medicine. Primary responsibilities: Daily Operations, Infrastructure and AVIT Support Manage, operate and maintain C-AIM’s AVIT, computing and infrastructure resources, including microaccess laboratories and AI simulation rooms, to ensure readiness for meetings, events, demonstrations, teaching, research activities and stakeholder engagements; Provide day-to-day technical support, troubleshooting and liaison with institutional teams, vendors and service providers for equipment setup, servicing, procurement and upgrades; Maintain inventories, usage records, documentation and operational trackers to support efficient centre operations, audit readiness and continuity of services. Behavioural, Communication and Social Science Research Support Support healthcare AI implementation studies that examine human-machine interaction, communication practices, user behaviour, trust, acceptability, adoption, workflow fit and outcomes-based evidence in clinical, educational or organisational settings; Assist with the design, rollout and monitoring of surveys, interviews, focus groups, observational studies, simulation-based studies and conversational analysis protocols related to AI use in healthcare; Coordinate participant or cohort recruitment, consent-related documentation, scheduling, data collection logistics and follow-up activities for behavioural, communication and social science research components; Prepare, clean, organise and analyse qualitative, quantitative or mixed-methods data, including survey responses, observational notes, transcripts, interaction logs and implementation outcome measures. Healthcare AI Implementation and Project Support Support strategic healthcare AI implementation projects by assisting with needs assessment, workflow mapping, stakeholder documentation, user feedback collection and translation of research findings into practical implementation recommendations; Assist with data preparation, processing, analysis, evaluation and documentation for AI-enabled healthcare projects, ensuring that technical outputs are interpreted alongside behavioral, communication and organizational considerations; Contribute to the development, testing and evaluation of AI/ML workflows, prototypes, dashboards or tools that support responsible deployment, monitoring or evaluation of AI applications in healthcare settings; Support deployment, testing and maintenance of AI/ML applications on suitable institutional or cloud-based platforms, in coordination with relevant technical, governance and stakeholder teams. Research Coordination, Documentation and Communication Prepare and maintain research protocols, study materials, implementation notes, project reports, presentation materials and progress updates for C-AIM projects; Coordinate communication across research teams, clinical or institutional collaborators, external partners, vendors and administrative units to support timely project delivery and clear stakeholder engagement; Support the preparation of grant applications, research proposals, conference materials, posters, manuscripts, ethics submissions and other outputs arising from healthcare AI implementation and social science research work. Research Administration, Compliance and Centre Support Handle procurement, purchase requests, vendor coordination, asset tracking and resource planning for both routine centre operations and research project needs; Support audits, compliance checks, institutional reporting and documentation processes to ensure alignment with NTU, C-AIM and project governance requirements; Assist with research and legal agreements, project records, ethics or governance submissions where applicable, and coordination of administrative workflows required for collaborative healthcare AI projects; Coordinate with finance, procurement, human resources, estates, IT and other administrative departments to resolve operational matters and support smooth centre functioning. Required Competencies and Qualifications: Bachelor’s (for Assistant) or Master’s (for Associate) degree in Social Sciences, Communications, Psychology, Behavioral Science, Sociology, Economics, Econometrics, Public Health, Health Services Research, Implementation Science, Health Informatics, Data Science, or a closely related discipline relevant to behavioral, communication and healthcare AI implementation research. Training or experience in behavioral, communication, psychology, social science or econometric research methods, including survey design, interviews, focus groups, observational studies, simulation-based studies, conversational analysis, implementation evaluation or mixed-methods research. Ability to support healthcare AI implementation studies examining human-machine interaction, user behavior, trust, acceptability, adoption, communication practices, workflow fit and outcomes-based evidence in healthcare, education or organizational settings. Competence in preparing, cleaning, organizing and analysing qualitative, quantitative or mixed-methods data, including survey responses, interview or focus group transcripts, observational notes, interaction logs and implementation outcome measures. Familiarity with statistical, qualitative or econometric analysis tools such as R, Python, Stata, SPSS, NVivo, ATLAS.ti, Excel or equivalent platforms is advantageous; willingness to learn additional data analysis or healthcare AI tools is expected. Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to prepare research protocols, study materials, reports, grant or proposal inputs, presentations, ethics documents and stakeholder-facing updates clearly and accurately. Good interpersonal and coordination skills, with the ability to liaise professionally with research teams, clinical or institutional collaborators, study participants, vendors and administrative units across multidisciplinary healthcare AI projects. Practical ability or willingness to support daily centre operations, including AVIT setup, equipment readiness, infrastructure coordination, inventory tracking, procurement documentation, audit preparation and liaison with vendors or institutional service teams. Experience or willingness to learn research administration processes, including participant or cohort recruitment, consent-related documentation, ethics or governance submissions, project reporting, compliance documentation, grant support and research agreement coordination. Strong organisational skills, attention to detail and interest in healthcare, AI in medicine, responsible AI implementation, digital health, health communication, behavioural science or health system improvement. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant-Associate--AI-in-Medicine_R00025438-2": {
      "title": "Research Assistant/Associate, AI in Medicine",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nCentre of AI in Medicine is a university-level research centre with the mission to bridge the gap between cutting-edge Artificial Intelligence (AI) technologies and practical applications in healthcare, The key objective is to spearheadresearch and development to revolutionise patient care and inform public health policies. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/c-aim We are seeking a Research Assistant / Research Associate to contribute towards the daily operational needs and strategic research priorities of the NTU Centre of AI in Medicine (C-AIM). The role will support the smooth running of C-AIM’s infrastructure, AVIT systems, administrative processes, procurement, audits, documentation, and coordination activities, ensuring that the Centre’s day-to-day functions are reliable, efficient, and responsive to project and stakeholder needs. In parallel, the candidate will provide data science and AI/ML modelling support for strategic healthcare AI projects, including clinical and biomedical data preparation, feature engineering, statistical modelling, machine learning model development, validation, performance evaluation, workflow prototyping, reproducible analysis, technical documentation, grant and proposal support, and coordination with internal and external collaborators. Through this dual operational and research-facing role, the candidate will help C-AIM translate AI innovations into practical healthcare applications that advance patient care, health system improvement, and responsible AI implementation in medicine. Primary Responsibilities: Daily Operations, Infrastructure and AVIT Support Manage, operate and maintain C-AIM’s AVIT, computing and infrastructure resources, including microaccess laboratories and AI simulation rooms, to ensure readiness for meetings, events, demonstrations, teaching, research activities and stakeholder engagements; Provide day-to-day technical support, troubleshooting and liaison with institutional teams, vendors and service providers for equipment setup, servicing, procurement and upgrades; Maintain inventories, usage records, documentation and operational trackers to support efficient centre operations, audit readiness and continuity of services. Data Science, AI/ML Modelling and Technical Research Support Support healthcare AI projects involving statistical modelling, machine learning, predictive analytics, natural language processing, multimodal data integration or other AI/ML approaches relevant to clinical, biomedical or health system applications; Assist with data extraction, cleaning, harmonisation, feature engineering, exploratory analysis, model training, validation, benchmarking, calibration and performance evaluation using appropriate statistical and machine learning methods; Develop, test and document reproducible analytical workflows, scripts, notebooks, pipelines, dashboards or prototypes to support AI/ML model development and evaluation in healthcare settings; Prepare technical summaries, model outputs, visualisations and interpretation notes to support research meetings, grant applications, project reports, manuscripts and stakeholder-facing communications. Healthcare AI Implementation and Project Support Support strategic healthcare AI implementation projects by assisting with needs assessment, workflow mapping, stakeholder documentation, user feedback collection and translation of research findings into practical implementation recommendations; Assist with data preparation, processing, statistical analysis, model development, validation, evaluation and documentation for AI-enabled healthcare projects, ensuring that technical outputs are robust, interpretable and aligned with clinical or implementation needs; Contribute to the development, testing and evaluation of AI/ML workflows, prototypes, dashboards or tools that support responsible deployment, monitoring or evaluation of AI applications in healthcare settings; Support deployment, testing and maintenance of AI/ML applications on suitable institutional or cloud-based platforms, in coordination with relevant technical, governance and stakeholder teams. Research Coordination, Documentation and Communication Prepare and maintain research protocols, study materials, implementation notes, project reports, presentation materials and progress updates for C-AIM projects; Coordinate communication across data science teams, clinical or institutional collaborators, technical partners, vendors and administrative units to support timely project delivery and clear stakeholder engagement; Support the preparation of grant applications, research proposals, conference materials, posters, manuscripts, ethics submissions and other outputs arising from healthcare AI, data science and AI/ML modelling work. Research Administration, Compliance and Centre Support Handle procurement, purchase requests, vendor coordination, asset tracking and resource planning for both routine centre operations and research project needs; Support audits, compliance checks, institutional reporting and documentation processes to ensure alignment with NTU, C-AIM and project governance requirements; Assist with research and legal agreements, project records, ethics or governance submissions where applicable, and coordination of administrative workflows required for collaborative healthcare AI projects; Coordinate with finance, procurement, human resources, estates, IT and other administrative departments to resolve operational matters and support smooth centre functioning. Required Competencies and Qualifications: Bachelor’s (for Research Assistant) or Master’s (for Research Associate) degree in Data Science, Statistics, Computer Science, Engineering, Biomedical Engineering, Health Informatics, Bioinformatics, Computational Biology, Applied Mathematics, Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, or a closely related quantitative discipline relevant to healthcare AI and AI/ML modelling. Training or experience in data science, statistical analysis, machine learning, predictive modelling, natural language processing, deep learning, biomedical data analysis, clinical data analytics or related AI/ML methods. Ability to support healthcare AI studies involving data preparation, feature engineering, model development, validation, benchmarking, calibration, performance evaluation, interpretability analysis and translation of technical outputs into actionable research insights. Competence in preparing, cleaning, organising and analysing structured or unstructured datasets, including clinical, biomedical, imaging, omics, text, survey, workflow, interaction-log or implementation outcome data where applicable. Proficiency or strong working familiarity with programming and data analysis tools such as Python, R, SQL, Git, Jupyter notebooks, machine learning libraries, statistical packages, visualisation tools or equivalent platforms is expected. Experience with reproducible analytical workflows, model documentation, experiment tracking, version control, data governance, privacy-aware analysis or deployment-oriented AI/ML workflows is advantageous. Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to prepare technical documentation, research protocols, analytical reports, grant or proposal inputs, presentations, ethics documents and stakeholder-facing updates clearly and accurately. Good interpersonal and coordination skills, with the ability to liaise professionally with research teams, clinical or institutional collaborators, technical partners, vendors and administrative units across multidisciplinary healthcare AI projects. Practical ability or willingness to support daily centre operations, including AVIT setup, equipment readiness, infrastructure coordination, inventory tracking, procurement documentation, audit preparation and liaison with vendors or institutional service teams. Strong organisational skills, attention to detail and interest in healthcare, AI in medicine, responsible AI implementation, digital health, clinical data science, biomedical AI, machine learning or health system improvement. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Learning-Strategist---Learning-Strategist--Centre-for-Innovation-in-Learning---NIE-_R00017190": {
      "title": "Senior Learning Strategist / Learning Strategist (Centre for Innovation in Learning) [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nABOUT THE NATIONAL INSTITUTE OF EDUCATION (NIE) The National Institute of Education (NIE), Singapore , is Singapore’s national teacher education institute, and we are proud to be an integral part of the nation’s education service. We play a key role in the preparation of teachers and in the provision of teacher professional and school leadership development programmes. We are committed to our vision of being An Institute of Distinction: Leading the Future of Education, and our mission to Inspire Learning, Transform Teaching and Advance Research . Read more about NIE here . We are seeking a pedagogically minded and dedicated Senior Learning Strategist / Learning Strategist. Reporting to the Learning Strategist Manager, the appointee collaborates with faculties to design and develop cutting-edge blended learning experiences, providing strategic guidance for implementing innovative digital teaching and learning practices across NIE. Additionally, the appointee will work closely with fellow Learning Strategists and the other teams in the department to research, develop, and present innovative and pedagogically sound design solutions to stakeholders, in pursuit of enhanced practice and outcomes. The candidate should be familiar with the training and adult education landscape, be adept at facilitation and possess a commitment to staying up to date on higher education best practices. This is a 2-year contract position. Responsibilities Build Evidence-Based Innovation in Teaching & Learning within NIE a) Collaborate with fellow Learning Strategists to: Research adult learning theories, strategies, data, and appropriate educational technology tools to design, develop, and facilitate impactful face-to-face and online tech-enhanced workshops for faculty. Assess the learning needs of IN-Learning specialists in learning design and emerging technology. Design, develop, and facilitate engaging initiatives to support IN-Learning specialists in building their expertise in learning design and emerging technology. b) Collaborate with NIE faculty to: Identify learning needs for courses they teach. Propose frameworks, new/enhanced learning outcomes, tech-enabled teaching and learning strategies, and assessments as part of course redesigning. Propose appropriate educational technology to overcome gaps and enhance the learning outcomes of the courses. Achieve constructive alignment of the learning outcomes with the learning activities and assessment in their courses. c) Collaborate with cross-functional teams to: Assess faculty capability development needs through qualitative and quantitative data analysis, to inform their work in designing, developing, and evaluating learner-centered blended learning experiences and fostering assessment literacy. Research, develop and present evidence-based and innovative design solutions with the project team to stakeholders. Research and evaluate frameworks and educational technology tools for implementation to optimize and innovate teaching, learning and assessment practices in NIE. Research, write grant proposals and develop tech-enabled learning solutions. Work together on initiatives with IN-Learning's Engagement, Planning and Research team to share learning sciences knowledge and improve practices institute-wide. Carry out action research by: conceptualizing frameworks and methodologies  designing evaluation instruments  gathering and analyzing data (e.g. Learning Analytics) formulating decisions to improve the effectiveness of learning experiences and our Capability Development initiatives Contribute to special projects on teaching and learning, as required. Keep Up with Learning Sciences and Innovative Teaching and Learning Practices Stay current on learning sciences, innovative teaching and learning practices in higher education (e.g., personalized learning, adaptive learning, e-assessment, hybrid learning, learning analytics, and Artificial Intelligence). Foster a culture of continuous learning within the team by providing opportunities for professional development and encouraging knowledge sharing. Requirements A University degree, preferably in Instructional Design, Education or Learning Sciences and Technologies. A master’s degree is preferred. A minimum of 2 years of experience in instructional design, teaching and learning, within a higher educational setting or with adult learners. Proven ability to manage successful learning projects. To be considered for the Senior Learning Strategist position, candidates should: Possess at least 5 years of experience in instructional design, teaching, learning, and the adult education landscape. Possess a proven track record of managing complex learning projects. Demonstrate experience in a mentorship role and in leading complex projects. Expert knowledge of applying Adult Learning theories in the design of Blended Learning experiences. Possess strong research skills. Proven track record in designing and facilitating faculty development workshops for diverse audiences. Possess strong written, verbal, and presentation skills. Strong knowledge of emerging educational technologies for teaching and learning. Excellent time management skills to meet multiple deadlines simultaneously and consistently deliver high-quality results. Excellent organizational and project management skills. Experience in facilitating both face-to-face and online sessions. Familiarity with Learning Management System and a demonstrated ability to rapidly learn new tools and processes with minimal support. Demonstrate excellent interpersonal skills and strong problem-solving abilities. Highly motivated, able to work independently yet also a strong team player. A strong desire to learn, acquire, and share new knowledge. Maintain a positive attitude and work effectively under pressure to meet deadlines. Closing Date The closing date of the advertisement is 12 August 2026. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Other Information NIE staff can take chartered buses at their own expense from or near their homes to the NIE campus. This is subject to availability of seats. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Novena-Campus-Singapore/Temporary-Senior-Executive--Programme-Shared-Services--LKCMedicine-_R00024398": {
      "title": "Temporary Senior Executive, Programme Shared Services [LKCMedicine]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (LKCMedicine) trains doctors who put patients at the centre of their exemplary care. The School, which offers both undergraduate and graduate programmes, is named after local philanthropist Tan Sri Dato Lee Kong Chian. Established in 2010 by Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, in partnership with Imperial College London, LKCMedicine aims to be a model for innovative medical education and a centre for transformative research. The School’s primary clinical partner is the National Healthcare Group, a leader in public healthcare recognised for the quality of its medical expertise, facilities and teaching. The School is transitioning to an NTU medical school ahead of the 2028 successful conclusion of the NTU-Imperial partnership to set up a Joint Medical School. In August 2024, we welcomed our first intake of the NTU MBBS programme, that has been recently enhanced to include themes like precision medicine and Artificial Intelligence (AI) in healthcare, with an expanded scope in the medical humanities. Graduates from the five-year undergraduate medical degree programme will have a strong understanding of the scientific basis of medicine, with an emphasis on technology, data science and the humanities. The Programme Shared Services (PSS) provides specialized research administration support to Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine’s 8 Research Programmes and their directors.  It sits within the ambit of Research Administration and Support Services Department under the Vice Dean of Research Office. The PSS team supports the various research programmes in their large grant applications, contracts management, visiting academics management and events planning.  This position is expected to work well and closely with the Grants Management, Contracts Management and Events Management teams to support the Research Programmes and Directors. Responsibilities: Provide administrative support for programme events, meetings, workshops, seminars and activities which includes booking and procurement of AVIT support, venues and catering, publicity of seminar programmes Work closely with the Programme Directors and the Grants team for large programme grant applications Support the Research Programmes and work closely with the Office of Faculty Affairs to administer Visiting Academics’ programmes and seminars Support ad-hoc Research Administration and Operation projects Requirements: Bachelor Degree in any discipline Minimum 3 of related working experience in preferably academic / research / healthcare industry Experience in project or research management and working on projects with many different facets preferred Demonstrated ability to build and maintain relationships with diverse stakeholders Strong problem solving and negotiation skills Experience in dealing with management and faculty preferred This is a temporary contract till 31 March 2027. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: LKC"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Human-Factors-_R00025434": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Human Factors)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAir Traffic Management Research Institute (ATMRI) is a research institute at Nanyang Technological University (NTU), Singapore, supported by the Civil Aviation Authority of Singapore (CAAS). The key objective of ATMRI is to support research and innovation in air traffic management. ATMRI focuses on developing practical and data-driven solutions for complex aviation systems, in close collaboration with industry and international partners. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/atmri . We are looking for a Research Fellow to conduct research on human factors and cognitive systems in air traffic management (ATM), with a focus on operator cognitive load, situational awareness, and decision-support interfaces for air traffic controllers. The role will involve designing and evaluating human-in-the-loop tools using methods such as eye-tracking, physiological sensing, and uncertainty visualization, contributing to the advancement of research and innovation at Nanyang Technological University. Key Responsibilities: Conduct research on human factors and cognitive systems approaches to support air traffic management studies and applications. Design, develop, and evaluate decision-support interfaces and operator-facing tools using operational and simulated data. Support research activities on controller cognitive load, situational awareness, and resilience under current and future ATM concepts. Work collaboratively with researchers and engineers to develop prototype solutions and human-in-the-loop evaluation frameworks. Conduct user studies and analyse results (e.g. eye-tracking, physiological sensing) to assess the performance and usability of developed tools in realistic operational scenarios. Prepare technical reports, research papers, and project deliverables, and participate in project meetings and reviews. Publish research findings in top-tier journals and conferences in relevant fields (e.g. human-computer interaction, human factors, ATM). Contribute to research proposals, technical documentation, and other project-related activities as required. Job Requirements: PhD qualification in Human-Computer Interaction, Cognitive Science, Human Factors, Air Traffic Management, Transport, or other related fields. At least one (1) year of relevant research experience in human factors, cognitive systems, or related technical research roles, ideally within transport, aviation, or other safety-critical operational domains. Familiarity with research related to cognitive load assessment, decision-support interfaces, or human-in-the-loop systems for complex operational environments (e.g. air traffic management, control rooms). Good written and oral communication skills, with the ability to prepare technical reports and academic publications. Proficiency in job-specific technical skills, including programming for research and data analysis purposes (e.g. Python or similar languages), experience with eye-tracking or physiological sensing methods, as well as strong numerical and analytical skills. Competent in general research-related skills and professional attributes, including problem-solving and analytical thinking. Strong interpersonal skills, with the ability to work independently and collaboratively, develop solutions under defined timelines, and demonstrate good organisational and time management skills. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Scientist--Electrical-Engineering--Computer-Engineering-Computer-Science-AI-Data-Science-_R00025432": {
      "title": "Research Scientist (Electrical Engineering /Computer Engineering/Computer Science/AI/Data Science)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Alibaba-NTU Global e-Sustainability CorpLab (ANGEL) represents a key collaboration between Alibaba Group and Nanyang Technological University (NTU). Supported by the Singapore RIE2025 Fund, ANGEL creates and deploys impactful green digital technologies for global sustainability. ANGEL’s mission aligns seamlessly with Singapore’s national objectives, such as the Singapore Green Plan 2030 and the Singapore Smart Nation Initiative. ANGEL’s work in developing sustainable and equitable digital solutions and promoting a sustainable and green lifestyle will contribute to a smaller carbon footprint. Its holistic approach will help to secure a brighter, more sustainable future for humanity.  We are seeking to hire a Research Scientist to support an advanced research programme on vector search on high-dimensional vectors. This role directly contributes to NTU’s mission of advancing cutting-edge AI technologies by developing next-generation methods that improve the performance, reliability, and efficiency of vector search systems. The Research Scientist will contribute to translating research outcomes into practical sustainability standards methodologies. Key Responsibilities: Develop quantitative sustainability indicators and performance metrics for sustainability living and smart communities. Design data-driven assessment methodologies for environmental, social, and governance (ESG) performance evaluation. Develop AI-enabled measurement and monitoring frameworks for sustainability applications. Build digital tools for sustainability data collection, validation, visualization, and reporting. Apply machine learning, optimization, and statistical analysis to evaluate sustainability performance. Design trustworthy AI methodologies to ensure transparency, robustness, fairness, and reproducibility in sustainability assessments. Conduct literature reviews, design experiments/surveys in sustainability, data collection and analysis, develop and test the statistical and computational models for the metrics. Coordinate with research team and communicate with collaborators Prepare research proposals, technical reports, scientific publications, arising from the research. Job Requirements: PhD in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, Computer Science, AI, Data Science, or a closely related discipline. Strong research background in machine learning, optimization, AI systems, or data analytics. Experience developing quantitative evaluation methodologies or performance metrics. Strong programming skills in Python and modern AI frameworks (e.g., PyTorch, Hugging Face). Experience with optimization algorithms, statistical modelling, or large-scale data analysis. Excellent scientific writing and publication record. Ability to work independently and collaborate across multidisciplinary teams. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant--Human-Computer-Interaction-Computer-Science-Information-Science-_R00025435": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (Human-Computer Interaction/Computer Science/Information Science)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nEstablished in 1992, the Wee Kim Wee School of Communication and Information (WKWSCI) is the only full-fledged communication and information school in Singapore. It is a world-class centre of excellence with an international faculty, state-of-the-art research facilities, and global institutional affiliations. The exceptional School, faculty and students have together made major impact in the spheres of communication and information, winning awards in creative, academic, journalistic and research arenas at the highest levels of international competitions. We are looking for a Research Assistant to contribute to a research project on Artificial Intelligence (AI) for mental health. Key Responsibilities: Assist in conducting research on social and emotional AI use and safety evaluation.  Contribute to publications in top-tier HCI journals, communication, and interdisciplinary venues Collaborate with students and interdisciplinary team members and build partnerships with external stakeholders such as community organisations and/or industry. Support lab development, including organising research activities, managing projects, and contributing to grant proposals. Job Requirements: Bachelor degree in Human-Computer Interaction, Computer Science, Information Science, or a related field. At least 1 year of relevant experience in doing research in a relevant field. Familiarity with social science theories, HCI, and well-being. Good written and oral communication skills. Proficiency in quantitative/statistical analysis and computational techniques. Ability to work independently and with interdisciplinary teams, excellent time management skills. ​ We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Linguistics--Singapore-Mandarin-Usage-Dictionary--_R00025431": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Linguistics (Singapore Mandarin Usage Dictionary))",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Humanities (SoH) at Nanyang Technological University (NTU), Singapore, brings together vibrant research and teaching across Chinese, English and literature, history, linguistics and multilingual studies, and philosophy. For more details, please visit https://www.ntu.edu.sg/soh . We are looking for a full-time Research Associate in Linguistics to support the MOE SSHR Thematic Grant project, Singapore Mandarin Usage Dictionary. The Research Associate will be a core member of the project team and will independently conduct literature review, linguistic analysis, corpus-based research, and cross-varietal comparison. Key Responsibilities: The role will involve providing linguistic input for annotation and computational modelling, interpreting corpus and model outputs, and using these findings to design, draft, and refine dictionary entries. The Research Associate will also coordinate annotation and quality assurance, maintain research documentation, guide student assistants, and contribute to project reports, publications, presentations, and other research activities. The appointee will work independently while collaborating closely with the PI, Co-PIs, computational researchers, and project collaborators. Job Requirements: Master’s degree in Linguistics, Chinese Linguistics, Applied Linguistics, Corpus Linguistics, Lexicography, or a related field Strong training in Chinese linguistic analysis, particularly in areas such as lexis, semantics, syntax, pragmatics, language variation, corpus linguistics, or lexicography High level of proficiency in written and spoken Chinese and English so as to support the technical components of the Grant project, Singapore Mandarin Usage Dictionary Experience in corpus-based research, linguistic annotation, lexical analysis, dictionary compilation, or related language research Ability to independently analyze linguistic data, interpret corpus and computational findings, and produce clear research outputs Strong analytical, writing, organizational, and quality assurance skills Ability to work independently and collaboratively and to guide student assistants Familiarity with Singapore Mandarin, other Mandarin varieties, Chinese dialects, multilingualism, corpus tools, or annotation platforms would be an advantage to support the technical components of the Grant project, Singapore Mandarin Usage Dictionary We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant--Natural-Language-Processing--Singapore-Mandarin-Usage-Dictionary--_R00025430-1": {
      "title": "Research Assistant (Natural Language Processing (Singapore Mandarin Usage Dictionary))",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Humanities (SoH) at Nanyang Technological University (NTU), Singapore, brings together vibrant research and teaching across Chinese, English and literature, history, linguistics and multilingual studies, and philosophy. For more details, please visit https://www.ntu.edu.sg/soh. We are looking for a full-time Research Assistant with a background in Natural Language Processing (NLP) to support the technical components of the MOE SSHR Thematic Grant project, Singapore Mandarin Usage Dictionary. The role will focus on corpus construction, including speech-to-text processing and transcription of spoken corpora, and on the training, fine-tuning, and evaluation of computational models (e.g., Word2Vec, BERT) for identifying lexical variation and region-specific features in Singapore Mandarin. The Research Assistant will be based in Singapore and work closely with the Principal Investigator, Co-PI, and collaborators. The position is offered on an initial contract of 18 to 24 months. Key Responsibilities: Support corpus construction, including speech-to-text processing and transcription of spoken corpora Perform data preprocessing, cleaning, and quality checks on written and spoken corpus data Contribute to the training, fine-tuning, and evaluation of computational models (e.g., Word2Vec, BERT) Implement models and carry out systematic performance evaluation Prepare model outputs for linguistic validation and dictionary integration Contribute to the technical development of the online dictionary platform, including database integration and search functions Document code, workflows, and datasets, and support other project-related tasks as assigned Job Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Computational Linguistics, Natural Language Processing, or a related field Technical hands-on experience in NLP or machine learning, including model training, fine-tuning, and evaluation Familiarity with NLP models and toolkits (e.g., Word2Vec, BERT) and with speech-to-text workflows Proficiency in Python and common machine learning / NLP libraries (e.g., PyTorch, scikit-learn) Good written and oral communication skills; proficiency in Mandarin Chinese so as to support the technical components of the Grant project, Singapore Mandarin Usage Dictionary Ability to work independently and collaboratively, meticulous with an eye for detail, and excellent organizational skills We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Associate--Robotics-_R00025422": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Robotics)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSchool of Electrical and Electronic Engineering is one of the founding Schools of the Nanyang Technological University. Built on a culture of excellence, the School is renowned for its high academic standards and research. With over 3,000 undergraduates students and 2,000 graduate students it is one of the largest EEE schools in the world and ranks 4th in the field of Electrical & Electronic Engineering in the 2025 QS World University Rankings by Subjects. Today, the School has become one of the world’s largest engineering schools that nurtures competent engineers and researchers. Each year, the School graduates over a thousand students who are ready to take on great ambitions and challenges. For more details, please view: https://www.ntu.edu.sg/eee The project aims to develop robust, intelligent and efficient navigation systems for inspection robots, enabling autonomous localization, decision-making, motion planning and safe navigation in complex, dynamic real-world environments. The Research Associate will support research on robot navigation, focusing on the integration of visual perception, localization, planning and navigation. The role will also investigate learning-based approaches, including diffusion models and reinforcement learning, for navigation decision-making, trajectory generation and adaptive robot behavior. Key Responsibilities: Design and develop navigation algorithms for inspection robots in complex and dynamic environments. Work on global and local motion planning, obstacle avoidance, trajectory generation and trajectory tracking for humanoid robots. Investigate diffusion models and diffusion-based policies for navigation planning, trajectory generation and action prediction. Apply reinforcement learning and/or imitation learning methods to improve navigation performance and adaptive robot behavior. Integrate visual navigation and planning modules with humanoid locomotion and whole-body control systems. Build and evaluate algorithms in simulation environments and on real-world humanoid robotic platforms. Contribute to publications and technical reports Assist in mentoring students and supporting research activities Job Requirements: Master’s degree in Robotics, Mechanical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Computer Science, or related fields Strong background in at least one of the following: robot motion planning and control; autonomous decision-making; robot localization and navigation. Experience in one or more of the following: path planning, motion planning, trajectory optimization or model predictive control; reinforcement learning, imitation learning or learning-based control; diffusion policies or generative decision-making; robotics physics simulators (e.g., Isaac Gym, MuJoCo, Gazebo) Proficiency in Python and/or C++ Experience with PyTorch or similar deep learning frameworks Strong problem-solving ability and hands-on implementation skills We regret to inform you that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Project-Officer--AI-in-Innovation-Strategy-_R00025414": {
      "title": "Project Officer (AI in Innovation Strategy)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Division of Strategy, International Business, and Entrepreneurship (SIE) at Nanyang Business School invites applications for a research position focused on strategy and innovation in an age of generative AI. The successful candidate will support large-scale data collection and analysis projects based on these topics. This role offers opportunities for cross-disciplinary collaboration with leading international institutions. Responsibilities: Support logistics and planning for field studies. Conduct large-scale data analysis using statistical modelling. Design, implement, and evaluate computational pipelines for data collection, processing, and analysis from diverse sources (e.g. qualitative interview data, quantitative performance data). Prepare high-quality research outputs, including peer-reviewed journal articles, technical reports, and data visualisations Requirements: Bachelor’s degree or higher in Data Science, Economics, Psychology, Computer Science, or related fields. Proficiency in statistical/econometric analysis and in R, Python, or other analysis tools. Experience in handling large datasets and applying advanced analytical methods Strong communication and collaboration skills A track record of research excellence. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Dean-s-Office-and-Global-Engagement--Office-for-Research---NIE-_R00025368": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Dean’s Office and Global Engagement (Office for Research) [NIE]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nABOUT THE NATIONAL INSTITUTE OF EDUCATION (NIE) The National Institute of Education (NIE), Singapore , is Singapore’s national teacher education institute, and we are proud to be an integral part of the nation’s education service. We play a key role in the preparation of teachers and in the provision of teacher professional and school leadership development programmes. We are committed to our vision of being An Institute of Distinction: Leading the Future of Education, and our mission to Inspire Learning, Transform Teaching and Advance Research . Read more about NIE here . NIE invites suitable applications for the position of Assistant Manager, Dean’s Office and Global Engagement with the Office for Research. The Dean's Office plays an integral role in the strategic communications and engagement efforts of OfR, effectively conveying its strategic positioning and policies to MOE, NIE, and other stakeholders. The office also advances NIE’s global leadership and reputation in education research by fostering strategic international partnerships, facilitating high-impact collaborations and strengthening NIE’s contributions to global educational knowledge and practice. As the Assistant Manager, Dean’s Office and Global Engagement, you will play a key support role in NIE’s global research engagement strategy, building sustainable partnerships with leading universities and research institutions, and supporting initiatives that position NIE as a global thought leader in education research, policy, and practice. You will also support in strategic communications and engagement efforts of OfR. This is a contract post till 31 Mar 2028. Responsibilities Support the Dean’s Office in advancing NIE’s global engagement objectives and strategic priorities. Provide support in strategic research matters, including collation of reports, requests and secretarial support for OfR management and other strategic meetings. Support in organising Programme Office Meetings and OfR events including strategic retreats, townhalls and outreach to Academic Departments. Assist in the implementation of NIE’s global research engagement plans, including coordination, partnership activities, and collaboration initiatives. Help identify productive relationships with universities, research institutes, governments, and international organisations. Support the preparation, review, and coordination of institutional agreements, such as MOUs and Research Collaboration Agreements, in consultation with relevant stakeholders. Assist NIE faculty in identifying international research opportunities and developing collaborations. Coordinate international research outreach activities, including symposia, conferences, visiting scholar programmes, and research dialogues. Coordinate and arrrange international research consultancies, capacity-building programmes, and strategic research partnerships. Track and monitor the progress and outcomes of international research partnerships, and maintain records and dashboards for reporting purposes. Provide administrative and operational support on governance, compliance, and cultural protocol matters in international engagements. Work closely Associate Dean, Global & Strategic Engagement, OfR and internal stakeholders to ensure smooth execution of global engagement activities and alignment with NIE goals. Collaborate with NIE Research Centres, Academic Departments, and administrative units to strengthen international research engagement and raise NIE’s global visibility. Any other duties as assigned by the reporting officer. Requirements       A University degree. Preferably with 3 years of working experience in an educational institution. Good understanding of global trends, and quick ability to understand research environments. Excellent interpersonal, negotiation and communication skills. Strong analytical, planning and organizational abilities, with experience in project and stakeholder management. Good writing skills. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced and dynamic environment often with tight timelines. Able to communicate professionally and work with faculty and staff across various administrative units. Able to monitor compliance in policies and uphold governance of policies. High level of professionalism, adaptability and discretion when handling sensitive or confidential information. Proficiency in MS office applications or project management tools is an advantage. Closing Date The closing date of the advertisement is 12 August 2026. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Other Information NIE staff can take chartered buses at their own expense from or near their homes to the NIE campus. This is subject to availability of seats. Hiring Institution: NIE"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Scientist--Advanced-Diamond-Synthesis-_R00023571": {
      "title": "Research Scientist (Diamond Synthesis and Device Fabrication)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-09\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nTemasek Laboratories@NTU (TL@NTU) is a premier research institute at Nanyang Technological University specializing in advanced defense and security technologies. The institute collaborates with external partners and stakeholders on cutting-edge research in strategic defense systems, advanced materials, power electronics, and semiconductor technologies. TL@NTU houses state-of-the-art cleanroom facilities, thermal evaporation systems, and electrical characterization equipment supporting mission-critical research initiatives. We are seeking a Research Scientist to lead device fabrication and electrical characterization for developing diamond-based semiconductor devices for next-generation defense electronics. Key Responsibilities: Lead cleanroom fabrication of diamond-based electronic devices, including photolithography, thin film deposition, etching, metallization, and device patterning Develop and optimize surface charge transfer doping of hydrogen-terminated diamond through thermal evaporation of transition metal oxide (TMO) films, including in-situ annealing protocols for formation of 2-dimensional hole gas (2DHG) channels Fabricate low-resistance ohmic contacts and develop process flows for integration of diamond into radiofrequency (RF) field effect transistors (FETs) and high-power electronic devices Conduct comprehensive electrical characterization, including sheet resistance, I-V and C-V measurements, Hall effect, contact resistance, and transport property analysis, and extract device parameters Verify and optimize the surface transfer doping mechanism and characterize diamond post-deposition to confirm that surface conductivity is maintained Operate, and where required install and commission, the Microwave Plasma Chemical Vapour Deposition (MPCVD) reactor and hydrogenation system, and optimize iterative growth protocols for electronic-grade single-crystal diamond Execute plasma hydrogen termination of grown crystals and verify hydrogenation effectiveness, including crystal face specificity Perform materials characterization using Raman spectroscopy, Atomic Force Microscopy (AFM), X-ray diffraction (XRD), and scanning electron microscopy (SEM) to establish quality feedback loops between synthesis, fabrication, and device performance Coordinate safe handling and transport of diamond wafers between synthesis and fabrication facilities and ensure adherence to project timelines Maintain detailed fabrication protocols, process and equipment documentation, and device characterization records Prepare technical reports and presentations for project deliverables and review meetings, and collaborate with external partners and collaborating institutions Job Requirements: PhD degree in Electrical Engineering, Materials Science, Physics, Applied Physics, or related field with specialization in semiconductor device fabrication and characterization Minimum 2-3 years of relevant experience in cleanroom device fabrication, preferably with wide-bandgap semiconductors or novel electronic materials Extensive hands-on experience with cleanroom processes including photolithography, thin film deposition (thermal evaporation, sputtering), etching, and metallization Strong expertise in electrical characterization techniques including I-V measurements, C-V profiling, Hall effect measurements, and device parameter extraction Knowledge of metal oxide thin film deposition and surface functionalization of semiconductors Experience with ohmic contact formation and contact resistance measurement techniques Understanding of semiconductor device physics, particularly field-effect transistors, surface conductivity mechanisms, and charge transfer processes Proficiency in device simulation tools and electrical measurement equipment (probe stations, parameter analyzers, etc.) Experience with diamond, SiC, GaN, or other wide-bandgap semiconductor devices is highly desirable Excellent written and oral communication skills with proven publication record in device physics or semiconductor technology Strong project management and organizational skills with demonstrated ability to meet strict deadlines Ability to work independently while collaborating effectively across multidisciplinary teams and multiple institutions Rigorous adherence to cleanroom protocols, safety procedures, and contamination control practices Prior experience with RF devices, power electronics, or high-voltage devices is an advantage We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Director--Infrastructure-Planning---Upgrading--M-E-_R00025086": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Infrastructure Planning & Upgrading (M&E)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNanyang Technological University (NTU) is a leading research-intensive university in Singapore, committed to excellence in education, research and innovation. We are inviting experienced and motivated individuals to join our Office of Development and Facilities Management (ODFM), which oversees the development, operation and maintenance of all University buildings and grounds in support of NTU’s academic, research and administrative functions. We are seeking a dynamic and experienced Assistant Director, Infrastructure Planning & Upgrading (M&E) to lead mechanical and electrical (M&E) infrastructure upgrading initiatives across the campus. This role offers the opportunity to drive large-scale projects, modernize critical systems, and contribute to the development of a future-ready and sustainable university environment. Key Responsibilities Plan and oversee multi-year M&E upgrading roadmap and budget aligned with asset lifecycle and campus master plan. Conduct asset condition assessments and establish renewal priorities based on risk, criticality and lifecycle considerations. Drive infrastructure planning initiatives that support sustainability and digital transformation goals. Lead the end-to-end implementation of M&E infrastructure projects, including design, procurement, construction and commissioning. Manage consultants and contractors to ensure projects are delivered safely, on time, within budget and in accordance with quality standards. Implement effective project governance, risk management and quality assurance practices throughout the project lifecycle. Integrate energy-efficient technologies and sustainable solutions into infrastructure upgrading projects. Identify opportunities to optimize energy performance and improve the operational efficiency of campus infrastructure. Requirements Degree in Mechanical Engineering, Building Services, Facilities Management or related discipline. At least 10 years of relevant experience in mechanical & electrical (M&E) engineering, facilities/infrastructure management, or building services. Proven experience in managing infrastructure upgrading or asset renewal projects in a large and complex environment. Good knowledge of M&E systems, including HVAC, electrical distribution, fire protection systems, lifts and building management systems. Strong understanding of infrastructure lifecycle management, asset renewal strategies and maintenance practices. Good knowledge of project management, budgeting, risk management and contract administration. Strong stakeholder management, communication and problem-solving skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities and deliver results in a dynamic environment. Familiarity with energy-efficient technologies, smart building solutions and sustainability initiatives will be advantageous. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Manager--Partnerships---Engagement_R00024089": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Partnerships & Engagement",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nResearch Centre for Residue and Toxic Industrial Waste Management (TREASURES) at NTU is seeking a dynamic, highly organized, and resourceful Assistant Manager, Partnerships & Engagement to join the team. This position plays a pivotal role in bridging the gap between cutting-edge academic research and real-world industrial application. As the Assistant Manager, you will have the exciting opportunity to drive strategic corporate partnerships, manage high-impact engagement events, coordinate collaborative grant funding initiatives, and shape the digital public face of the centre. If you are passionate about science communication, stakeholder engagement, and research administration, we invite you to apply. Key Responsibilities: Event & Workshop Management: Spearhead the end-to-end planning and execution of industrial engagement events, including large-scale workshops, seminars, and targeted industry visits.  Digital Communications: Manage, maintain, and continuously update the research centre’s website, ensuring that news, upcoming events, and key research milestones are communicated effectively to an external audience. Stakeholder & Grant Coordination: Act as the primary administrative liaison for industrial partners and corporate stakeholders. Liaise with external Institutes of Higher Learning (IHLs) and industrial partners on grant funding-related matters to facilitate joint research collaborations.  Secretariat & Administrative Support: Provide vital day-to-day support for industry-focused meetings and advisory boards, including minute-taking, data gathering, and the preparation of management reports and presentation slides. Information Management: Handle confidential and sensitive industrial data or collaboration agreements with the highest level of discretion. Requirements: A Bachelor’s degree from a recognized institution in Business, Communications, STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering, Mathematics), or a related discipline. At least 3 to 4 years of relevant work experience in event management, corporate communications, or industrial liaison roles, ideally within a fast-paced or complex organization. Experience working within an Institute of Higher Learning (IHL) or a research institute is highly advantageous. Strong organizational and time management skills, with a proven track record of managing logistics for diverse audiences. Excellent verbal and written communication skills, specifically the ability to translate complex research or technical concepts into accessible language for industrial partners. Proficiency in website content management and Microsoft Office applications. A proactive, resourceful, and adaptable approach to work, with strong interpersonal skills to liaise effectively with academics and corporate executives. Relevant work experience in Building and Environment Sector is preferred. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Assistant-Director--Business-Operations--Finance--Marketing---Strategy-_R00025166": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Business Operations (Finance, Marketing & Strategy)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAbout NTU Nanyang Technological University (NTU) is a leading research-intensive university, recognised internationally for its excellence in education, research, and innovation. NTU fosters a collaborative and inclusive work environment that supports professional growth and continuous learning. About the Role We are seeking a dynamic and strategic professional to join as Assistant Director, overseeing communications, strategy, outreach, and operations for the institute. This role offers the opportunity to work closely with leadership to shape institutional positioning, drive impactful initiatives, and engage a wide range of stakeholders. Why Join Us Opportunity to work at the intersection of academia, policy, and industry Exposure to senior leadership and high-impact initiatives Collaborative and dynamic work environment Key Responsibilities Strategic Leadership & Institute Development Support the Director in shaping and executing IBI’s medium- and long-term strategies to strengthen Singapore’s international trading ecosystem Translate institutional and national objectives into clear plans, initiatives, and KPIs, ensuring effective execution and measurable outcomes Identify strategic opportunities for growth, partnerships, and new initiatives that enhance IBI’s relevance and impact Industry Development & Corporate Engagement Lead and deepen strategic partnerships with government agencies, corporate partners, and industry stakeholders Drive initiatives that enhance industry collaboration, experiential learning, and ecosystem development Represent IBI as a credible and trusted partner within the international trading and policy ecosystem, both locally and globally Student, Alumni & Talent Development Oversee initiatives that enhance student engagement, industry exposure, and career readiness across the programme lifecycle Guide the development and continuous improvement of platforms and programmes supporting internships, careers, mentorship, and alumni engagement Leverage alumni networks to strengthen industry ties and long-term ecosystem outcomes Fundraising & Financial Sustainability Ensure IBI remains financially sustainable and self-funding through effective corporate partner engagement Cultivate, retain, and expand corporate funding relationships by demonstrating clear value, relevance, and impact Oversee contribution agreements, funding initiatives, and donor-related engagements in alignment with strategic priorities Strategic Communications, Branding & Media Oversight Provide strategic direction on communications, branding, and outreach to position IBI as a leading hub for international trading education and engagement Oversee media, digital, and public engagement efforts, ensuring clear, consistent, and responsible messaging Manage reputational risks and advise leadership on communication strategies and public positioning Events, Engagement & Executive Support Conceptualise and oversee high-impact events, including industry dialogues, conferences, experiential learning programmes, and donor engagements Ensure events are strategically leveraged for visibility, partnerships, fundraising, and thought leadership Support senior leadership in strategic engagements, external representation, and VIP or high-level stakeholder interactions Governance, Planning & Performance Management Oversee planning, reporting, and governance processes, including KPIs linked to student outcomes, partnerships, and funding Ensure compliance with institutional, donor, and government requirements, including audit readiness Support continuous improvement of programmes, processes, and operational effectiveness Stakeholder, Team & Vendor Management Work effectively across the university ecosystem, including NBS, Finance, UAO, CAO, and other units, to ensure alignment and smooth execution Influence and align stakeholders in a matrixed environment without direct authority Manage external vendors and service providers to ensure quality delivery and value for money Provide guidance, mentorship, and leadership to team members, fostering a collaborative and high-performance culture Requirements IBI aims to provide a well-qualified talent pipeline for and build a strong linkage between the university and the international industry. It is looking for an Assistant Director (AD) who will work closely with various parts of the university and the industry to achieve its goals. This position provides the platform for the AD to play an important part in creating future leaders in the international industry, and to exert his or her abilities to build a strong linkage between the university and the industry.  The candidate should have: A good bachelor’s degree and proven high quality academic achievements At least 12-15 years of work experience, prior relevant experience will be an added advantage Knowledge and experience in business development and programme/operations management Strong strategic thinking and possess an analytical mind Excellent writing, communication and organisational skills Confident and proactive with demonstrated dynamism and resourcefulness in problem solving Ability to work with people of various levels and cultures, with excellent interpersonal skills Good commercial understanding of the local marketplace, coupled with an ability to establish wide networks and strong relationships with management of different companies Strong influencing skills, with a proven ability to provide pragmatic solutions Ability to proactively identify and prioritise tasks and be able to escalate matters of significance while retaining the responsibility for them We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Executive--Administrative-Support_R00025420-1": {
      "title": "Senior Executive, Administrative Support",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNanyang Technological University is a leading global university recognised for excellence in education and research. Nanyang Business School (NBS) is one of Asia’s premier business schools, committed to delivering impactful education and driving innovation in teaching and engagement. This incumbent is part of Nanyang Business School Corporate Services - Academic Support Unit that is dedicated to assisting faculty with research and teaching-related administrative tasks. The team aims to excel operationally by establishing a service centre focused on customer satisfaction and faculty support. This role will function as the primary contact for faculty regarding all administrative aspects of research and teaching activities. Job Responsibilities: Central / Cross Division Administrative Support Act as the main hub for the processing of faculty pre-travel requests, expense claims, and reimbursements. Provide proper and timely processing of expenses and claims incurred by faculty. Assist with purchases in accordance with NTU procurement policies and guidelines. Assist in budget planning for faculty-related expenses. Proper filing and accounting of revenue and expenditure for periodic financial reporting. Assist in the organisation of events such as seminars, workshops, and retreats, including logistical arrangements, budget monitoring, and smooth on-site execution. Support course coordinators in the submission of course outline revisions through the curriculum management application (CMA) platform. Provide support to divisions’ research centres. Support activities related to assessments (e.g., quizzes) and examination invigilation. Other tasks assigned by ASU Lead as required Job Requirements: Minimally a Diploma in Business Administration, or related field. Degree in Business Administration, or related field, is preferred. Minimum 5 years of working experience in an administrative role. Relevant working experience in the education sector will be advantageous. Strong proficiency in MS Office suite, and online productivity tools. Good written and verbal communication skills. Able to work individually and collaborate with others as a team Strong planning, organisational and problem-solving skills Independent and possess strong multi-tasking abilities Meticulous and attentive to detail We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Civil-Infrastructure-Monitoring-Using-_R00025405": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Civil Infrastructure Monitoring Using Distributed Sensing)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe School of Civil and Environmental Engineering (CEE) is a leading school for Sustainable Built Environment. Our mission in research is to achieve excellence by providing a conducive and intellectually stimulating environment to enable high quality work in strategic directions that are of significant impact to industry, science and technology. For more details, please view https://www.ntu.edu.sg/cee. We are looking for a Research Fellow, Civil Infrastructure Monitoring Using Distributed Sensing to advance scalable monitoring of bridges, tunnels, railroads, and roadway structures using distributed sensing technologies. The role will focus on distributed acoustic sensing on pre-existing telecom fiber networks, mobile sensing using vehicle fleets, multi-modal data fusion, and structural system identification through lab-scale and field experiments. Key Responsibilities: Develop algorithms for guided-wave analysis, response analysis, sensor fusion, and system identification using distributed and multi-modal sensing data. Design and execute lab-scale experiments to study structural response and validate distributed sensing methodologies. Plan and conduct field deployments on bridges, railroads, and roadway structures using Distributed Acoustic Sensing and Distributed Mobile Sensing (DAS) on telecom fiber networks and mobile sensing platforms. Build data processing pipelines for DAS and vehicle-based sensing datasets, including quality control, signal processing, and feature extraction. Integrate distributed sensing with complementary sensing modalities for infrastructure diagnostics, damage assessment, and performance monitoring. Prepare journal papers, conference presentations, technical reports, and proposal inputs with the PI and external collaborators. Mentor graduate students and contribute to collaborative research activities that advance the group's infrastructure monitoring agenda. Job Requirements : PhD in Civil/Structural Engineering, Engineering Mechanics, Electrical/Computer Engineering, Applied Physics, Computer/Data Science, Optical Engineering, or a related field. Strong research record in distributed fiber-optic sensing, structural health monitoring, structural dynamics, guided waves, system identification, or infrastructure monitoring. Experience with DAS or other distributed fiber-optic sensing technologies, including data processing, analysis, or deployment, is highly desirable. Proficiency in Python, C++, or Julia, with strong signal processing, numerical modeling, and data analysis skills; experience with Git-based workflows and AI/ML for science is a plus. Hands-on experience in structural testing or field experimentation, including modal testing, acoustic emission, ultrasonic testing, or related methods, is advantageous. Good written and oral communication skills, with the ability to publish high-quality research and work collaboratively with students and external partners. Ability to work independently, manage multiple research tasks, and engage in laboratory and fieldwork in a fast-paced research environment. We regret to inform that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Director--Centre-for-African-Studies_R00025418": {
      "title": "Director, Centre for African Studies",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nNTU-SBF Centre for African Studies (CAS), which is overseen by CAS Advisory Board, is a trilateral platform with government, business and academia to promote knowledge and expertise on Africa among Asian businesses and policymakers, to accelerate the creation of deeper economic and policy links between Africa and Asia. The Director, CAS jointly reports to the Chairman of the Advisory Board, CAS and Dean, Nanyang Business School (NBS), with a matrix reporting to Associate Dean, Research, Nanyang Business School As the Centre Director, this role oversees all activities for CAS, ensures the alignment of CAS’ development to its mission, drives the strategic vision for the centre and assists in establishing CAS’s presence locally, as well as internationally. The incumbent will develop and implement strategies to drive deeper collaborations between African and Singaporean companies, as well as to work closely with NBS faculty members to develop thought leadership in the area. Responsibilities: Centre Strategy Planning and Strategic Collaborations Work closely with the Advisory Board and NBS Senior Management to define and execute CAS’ strategic vision. Develop and deliver strategic road map to strengthen collaborations between African and Singaporean companies. Identify opportunities, assess risks and implement mitigation strategies to support sustainable growth and impact. Outreach & Industry Engagement Lead outreach and industry engagement initiatives in line with the Centre’s strategy. Build and maintain a strong network of corporate, government and ecosystem partners. Create and curate platforms to deepen relationships and mutual understanding between African and Singaporean businesses. Thought Leadership Partner with NBS faculty to drive practice-oriented thought leadership relevant to Africa-Singapore business collaboration. Lead end-to-end thought leadership delivery, including but not limited to content development, stakeholder engagement, copyright management and distribution. Expand visibility and impact of the Centre’s thought leadership through relevant platforms and channels. Governance Provide day-to-day leadership of the Centre, ensuring delivery against strategic and operational plans. Oversee resource allocation, financial management, budgeting and performance monitoring. Ensure full compliance with governance and reporting requirements Establish and maintain effective governance processes and workflows. Be accountable for achieving KPIs set by the Advisory Board, NBS Senior Management Revenue Generation & Fundraising Develop and execute a clear roadmap toward financial sustainability and self-funding. Leverage partnerships and other monetization avenues Lead business development efforts, engaging a multitude of stakeholder Operational Excellence Oversee planning, budgeting and delivery of CAS initiatives and events. Ensure operational excellence and efficiency in the Centre’s overall functioning. Maintain an up-to-date Centre activities calendar aligned with Centre’s mission and vision . Requirements: Bachelor’s Degree PhD or DBA qualifications would be viewed favorably A minimum of 10 years of relevant experience Demonstrated experience in driving successful partnerships and/or industry engagement Demonstrated experience and working knowledge of companies from Africa Established networks and contacts in this area would be a distinct advantage Experience in outreach and running engagement events Familiarity and working experience with faculty members and/or an institution of higher learning would be an advantage Experience working on industry white papers and projects would be preferred Strategic thinking capabilities Self-driven and yet able to work in a team Good organisational skills Strong interpersonal and communication skills We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Trust-Technologies-_R00025413": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Trust Technologies)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNanyang Technological University’s National Centre for Research in Digital Trust (DTC) is a Trust Technology Research Centre to execute a national program to help put Singapore into a strong trust hub. The key objective is to support efforts to create a trusted digital environment for people and businesses in the digital transformation by providing businesses and consumers with greater assurance and confidence as they digitalize.  The successful applicant is expected to be involved in research and development on Trust Technology including topics such as Trustworthy computation, Trustworthy AI Assurance and Insurance, Quantum Trust, Privacy-preserving Machine Learning, Privacy-preserving Multi-party Computation, Verifiable Computation, Trustworthy Systems, Adversarial Machine Learning, Assessing Trustworthiness of AI models etc.  Key Responsibilities:  Responsible for research and development of Privacy Enhancing Technology under real using scenarios, e.g.  for Law Enforcement units, such as Quantum-Resilient Encryption, Privacy-preserving Financial Investigations, Graph Analytics, Criminal Network Discovery, Suspicious Activity Detection, Digital Content Provenance and Authenticity, etc., which are important components to strengthen trust, security, and resilience in the digital economy. Responsible for technologies system development/implementation, and delivery working prototypes/demo. Lead/Involved in research/industrial projects. Prepare reports and scientific papers. Job Requirements: Ph.D. degree in Computer Science, Mathematics, Information Theory, Cybersecurity, Electrical Engineering, or a related field. Strong publication record in top-tier conferences and journals related to AI, security, privacy, trustworthy computing, and PQC. Solid background in Privacy Preserving technologies, including Post Quantum Cryptography (PQC), Homomorphic Encryption, Secure Computation. Experience with deep learning frameworks such as PyTorch or TensorFlow. Proficiency in programming languages, e.g. C/C++, Python. Experience with Machine learning technologies (e.g., LLM, and Machine Learning) is an advantage Experience with Hardware, e.g., FPGA acceleration, is an advantage. Excellent communication skills, self-motivation, and the ability to deliver high-quality research outcomes under tight schedules. Ability to work independently as well as collaboratively in a multidisciplinary research team. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Main-Campus-Singapore/Research-Fellow--Trust-Technologies-_R00025415": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Trust Technologies)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nNanyang Technological University’s National Centre for Research in Digital Trust (DTC) is a Trust Technology Research Centre to execute a national program to help put Singapore into a strong trust hub. The key objective is to support efforts to create a trusted digital environment for people and businesses in the digital transformation by providing businesses and consumers with greater assurance and confidence as they digitalize.  The successful applicant is expected to be involved in research and development on Trust Technology including topics such as Trustworthy computation, Trustworthy AI Assurance and Insurance, Quantum Trust, Privacy-preserving Machine Learning, Privacy-preserving Multi-party Computation, Verifiable Computation, Trustworthy Systems, Adversarial Machine Learning, Assessing Trustworthiness of AI models etc.  Key Responsibilities:  Responsible for research and development of Privacy Enhancing Technology under real using scenarios, e.g.  for Law Enforcement units, such as Quantum-Resilient Encryption, Privacy-preserving Financial Investigations, Graph Analytics, Criminal Network Discovery, Suspicious Activity Detection, Digital Content Provenance and Authenticity, etc., which are important components to strengthen trust, security, and resilience in the digital economy. Responsible for technologies system development/implementation, and delivery working prototypes/demo. Lead/Involved in research/industrial projects. Prepare reports and scientific papers. Job Requirements: Ph.D. degree in Computer Science, Mathematics, Information Theory, Cybersecurity, Electrical Engineering, or a related field. Strong publication record in top-tier conferences and journals related to AI, security, privacy, trustworthy computing, and PQC. Solid background in Privacy Preserving technologies, including Post Quantum Cryptography (PQC), Homomorphic Encryption, Secure Computation. Experience with deep learning frameworks such as PyTorch or TensorFlow. Proficiency in programming languages, e.g. C/C++, Python. Experience with Machine learning technologies (e.g., LLM, and Machine Learning) is an advantage Experience with Hardware, e.g., FPGA acceleration, is an advantage. Excellent communication skills, self-motivation, and the ability to deliver high-quality research outcomes under tight schedules. Ability to work independently as well as collaboratively in a multidisciplinary research team. We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: NTU"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Novena-Campus-Singapore/Research-Assistant-Associate--Cardiometabolic-Medicine--LKCMedicine-_R00024301": {
      "title": "Research Assistant/Associate, Cardiometabolic Medicine [LKCMedicine]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-03\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (LKCMedicine) trains doctors who put patients at the centre of their exemplary care. The School, which offers both undergraduate and graduate programmes, is named after local philanthropist Tan Sri Dato Lee Kong Chian. Established in 2010 by Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, in partnership with Imperial College London, LKCMedicine aims to be a model for innovative medical education and a centre for transformative research. The School’s primary clinical partner is the National Healthcare Group, a leader in public healthcare recognised for the quality of its medical expertise, facilities and teaching. The School is transitioning to an NTU medical school ahead of the 2028 successful conclusion of the NTU-Imperial partnership to set up a Joint Medical School. In August 2024, we welcomed our first intake of the NTU MBBS programme, that has been recently enhanced to include themes like precision medicine and Artificial Intelligence (AI) in healthcare, with an expanded scope in the medical humanities. Graduates from the five-year undergraduate medical degree programme will have a strong understanding of the scientific basis of medicine, with an emphasis on technology, data science and the humanities. Assistant Professor Lynn Yap is looking for a motivated Research Assistant/ Research Associate to join her laboratory at the Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (Novena), a medical school in Nanyang Technological University (NTU). A/Prof Yap laboratory is working on the field of regenerative cardiology and metabolic disorders, where the team is interested in the basic and translational cardiometabolic research. The laboratory is focusing on regenerative cardiology using stem cell therapy to investigate cardio-immunology regeneration. We work with pluripotent stem cells and cardiovascular progenitor-mediated repair of myocardial infarction in small (rodents) and large (pigs) animal models. When transplanted into the animals, these progenitor cells engrafted, long-term survived and avoided ventricular arrhythmia in the animal. Therefore, providing a potential cellular therapy product for ischemic heart disease patients. In addition, we are interested in uncovering the molecular mechanism of cardiac regeneration, human graft maturation and host immunology in the heart using disruptive technologies and inventions. Lynn Yap’s laboratory is pursuing medical innovations by integrating science, engineering and technology to positively impact patients’ lives. Therefore, this role will provide an exciting opportunity for the individual to learn and experience collaborative academic/industry research and play an important role in impacting patients’ lives. For more details, please view https://dr.ntu.edu.sg/entities/person/Lynn-Yap We are looking for a motivated Research Assistant to join a collaborative project by Assistant Professor Lynn Yap (Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine, Novena campus). The role will focus on performing cellular and molecular experiments and animal models. Responsibilities: Conduct accurate monitoring, documenting and reporting of experimental results Assist in experiments including stem cell culture, western blotting, molecular biology, microscopy, histology, flow cytometry and bioinformatics. Assist in large animal study and IACUC revisions Assist in the general upkeep of laboratory needs, maintain safety protocols, risk assessments, lab audits and management of inventories Perform other related duties related to the work describe herein or assigned by the supervisor Requirements: Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Sciences/Life Sciences/ Data Science/Immunology with at least 2 year of work experience in a research environment. Good written and oral communication skills Demonstrated knowledge, skills, and expertise in supporting various research activities including molecular and cell biology, histology, flow cytometry and microscopy. Experience with stem cell biology and immunology. Strong interpersonal skills and a strong team player who is organized, energetic, open-minded, highly motivated, and able to multi-task and work collaboratively in a diverse team. RCULA certification and experience with animal studies will be an advantage. Entry level candidates are welcome to apply We regret that only shortlisted candidates will be notified. Hiring Institution: LKC"
    },
    "https://ntu.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/Careers/job/NTU-Novena-Campus-Singapore/Senior-Research-Fellow-in-Cardiometabolic-Medicine--LKCMedicine-_R00025404-1": {
      "title": "Senior/Research Fellow in Cardiometabolic Medicine [LKCMedicine]",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-03\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Description The Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (LKCMedicine) trains doctors who put patients at the centre of their exemplary care. The School, which offers both undergraduate and graduate programmes, is named after local philanthropist Tan Sri Dato Lee Kong Chian. Established in 2010 by Nanyang Technological University, Singapore, in partnership with Imperial College London, LKCMedicine aims to be a model for innovative medical education and a centre for transformative research. The School’s primary clinical partner is the National Healthcare Group, a leader in public healthcare recognised for the quality of its medical expertise, facilities and teaching. The School is transitioning to an NTU medical school ahead of the 2028 successful conclusion of the NTU-Imperial partnership to set up a Joint Medical School. In August 2024, we welcomed our first intake of the NTU MBBS programme, that has been recently enhanced to include themes like precision medicine and Artificial Intelligence (AI) in healthcare, with an expanded scope in the medical humanities. Graduates from the five-year undergraduate medical degree programme will have a strong understanding of the scientific basis of medicine, with an emphasis on technology, data science and the humanities. Assistant Professor Lynn Yap is looking for a motivated Senior/Research Fellow to join her laboratory at the Lee Kong Chian School of Medicine (Novena), a medical school in Nanyang Technological University (NTU). A/Prof Yap laboratory is working on the field of regenerative cardiology and metabolic disorders, where the team is interested in the basic and translational cardiometabolic research. The laboratory is focusing on regenerative cardiology using stem cell therapy to investigate cardio-immunology regeneration. We work with pluripotent stem cells and cardiovascular progenitor-mediated repair of myocardial infarction in small (rodents) and large (pigs) animal models. When transplanted into the animals, these progenitor cells engrafted, long-term survived and avoided ventricular arrhythmia in the animal. Therefore, providing a potential cellular therapy product for ischemic heart disease patients. In addition, we are interested in uncovering the molecular mechanism of cardiac regeneration, human graft maturation and immunology of the heart using disruptive technologies and inventions. Lynn Yap’s laboratory is pursuing medical innovations by integrating science, engineering and technology to positively impact patients’ lives. Therefore, this role will provide an exciting opportunity for the individual to learn and experience collaborative academic/industry research and play an important role in impacting patients’ lives. For more details, please view https://dr.ntu.edu.sg/entities/person/Lynn-Yap The selected candidate will perform a variety of functions related to research under the supervision of the Principal Investigator or her designate, including but not limited to the following: Conduct accurate monitoring, documenting and reporting of experimental results Present and communicate effectively the research findings Assist with figures and manuscript writing for publications Mentor the research assistants and PhD students Perform and troubleshoot wet bench experiments including stem cell culture, western blotting, molecular biology, microscopy, histology, and flow cytometry Involved in downstream bioinformatics analysis Willing to learn mouse myocardial infarction Lead large pig myocardial infarction study with collaborators Perform other related duties related to the work describe herein or assigned by the supervisor Required educational qualification, experience, skills and competencies: Ph.D. or equivalent degree with strong background and proven track record across stem cell biology, cardiology, RNA biology, functional genomics and/or immunology with at least 2 year of work experience in a research environment. Good written and oral communication skills Track record of high-quality publications Demonstrated knowledge, skills, and expertise in independent scientific research including molecular and cell biology, histology, flow cytometry and microscopy. Experience with cardiac biology, bioinformatics (scRNAseq, spatial transcriptomics etc) or immunology. Strong interpersonal skills and a strong team player who is organized, energetic, open-minded, highly motivated, and able to multi-task and work collaboratively in a diverse team. Ability to work independently, develop solutions under strict timelines and meticulous. Required to mentor and train PhD students, interns and RAs Experience with cardiac myocardial infarction in large or small animals is preferred Experience with mRNA and LNP technology will be welcome RCULA certification and experience with animal studies will be required. Entry level candidates are welcome to apply Hiring Institution: LKC"
    },
